1
00:00:00,398 --> 00:00:02,945
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:02,976 --> 00:00:07,467
الحمدلله والصلوة وسلام على سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

3
00:00:08,578 --> 00:00:15,947
Chapter 01: On the command of Jihad(جهاد) against the non-believers and its mandate,

4
00:00:16,622 --> 00:00:20,240
and the stern warning against those, who don’t practice Jihad(جهاد).

5
00:00:21,655 --> 00:00:24,371
Command to fight. Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

6
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:30,577
كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌ لَكُمْ ۖ

7
00:00:30,878 --> 00:00:37,742
وَعَسَىٰ أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئًا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ ۖ

8
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:44,454
وَعَسَىٰ أَنْ تُحِبُّوا شَيْئًا وَهُوَ شَرٌّ لَكُمْ ۗ

9
00:00:44,732 --> 00:00:50,215
وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ۞

10
00:00:51,374 --> 00:00:55,539
Fighting has been enjoined upon you, while it is hateful to you,

11
00:00:56,597 --> 00:00:59,853
but perhaps you hate a thing, and it is good for you,

12
00:01:00,392 --> 00:01:03,543
and perhaps you love a thing, and it is bad for you.

13
00:01:03,902 --> 00:01:06,531
And Allah knows while, you know not.

14
00:01:08,164 --> 00:01:17,366
Now don't think that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم we're looking forward to

15
00:01:17,898 --> 00:01:22,307
Yani(يعني) Qital(قتال) and asking for it.

16
00:01:23,559 --> 00:01:29,200
Fighting is something that is naturally disliked to a human heart.

17
00:01:32,285 --> 00:01:36,824
In general, there are some people, who love the adventure of it.

18
00:01:42,016 --> 00:01:46,468
But the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم they followed Rasool Ullah

19
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:50,542
You had a lot of people who don't like Jihad(جهاد).

20
00:01:51,226 --> 00:01:54,281
and this is with all of Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah even with Musa عليه السّلام,

21
00:01:54,331 --> 00:01:56,450
and with Talut(طالوت), and you know,the story of Talut(طالوت).

22
00:01:56,546 --> 00:02:01,632
They were asking for it and when Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told them to fight, they backed out of it.

23
00:02:02,442 --> 00:02:03,802
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

24
00:02:03,866 --> 00:02:05,401
كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌ لَكُمْ

25
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:10,674
But then Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says that you might dislike something, but it's good for you.

26
00:02:11,046 --> 00:02:13,058
And you might like something and it is not good for you.

27
00:02:13,809 --> 00:02:17,488
So the Sahabah(صحابه) were always willing to go with what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells them,

28
00:02:17,670 --> 00:02:20,724
is better than what their whims would tell them is better.

29
00:02:20,971 --> 00:02:22,385
And that's the thing about the Sahabah(صحابه).

30
00:02:22,465 --> 00:02:23,517
They do not follow Hawa(هواء).

31
00:02:24,756 --> 00:02:27,645
They do not follow their whims and desires.

32
00:02:28,702 --> 00:02:30,169
And that is the meaning of submission.

33
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:38,902
Ibrahim عليه السّلام, when he saw a dream that he is slaughtering his son Ismail عليه السّلام.

34
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:45,732
He went, grabbed the knife places his son under his knee and was about to slaughter him.

35
00:02:45,785 --> 00:02:47,890
What Allah عزَّوَجل called that posture?

36
00:02:49,105 --> 00:02:52,152
فَلَمَّا أَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهُ لِلْجَبِينِ

37
00:02:52,263 --> 00:02:53,263
Allah called it Islam

38
00:02:54,351 --> 00:02:58,329
that pasture, when Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was holding the knife, about to slaughter his son.

39
00:02:58,709 --> 00:03:00,349
Allah called it Islam(إسلام)!

40
00:03:01,028 --> 00:03:02,282
Because that's the meaning of Islam,

41
00:03:02,576 --> 00:03:06,495
you submit to what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells you whether you like it or not,

42
00:03:07,306 --> 00:03:08,883
whether it pleases you or not,

43
00:03:09,629 --> 00:03:11,470
whether it satisfies your Hawaa(هواء) or not.

44
00:03:12,244 --> 00:03:14,758
You do it not because you like it,

45
00:03:15,252 --> 00:03:18,913
not because you feel like doing it.

46
00:03:20,031 --> 00:03:21,904
But because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ wants you to do it.

47
00:03:23,278 --> 00:03:25,515
So Allah called that Islam, that is submission.

48
00:03:28,415 --> 00:03:32,455
And fight in the cause of Allah and know that the Allah is hearing and knowing.

49
00:03:32,717 --> 00:03:36,693
It is in Surah Baqarah(سورة ألبقرة), Ayah(آية) Verse 244,

50
00:03:38,317 --> 00:03:39,618
Al-Baqarah(ألبقرة) Verse 251:

51
00:03:41,051 --> 00:03:52,456
مَنْ ذَا الَّذِي يُقْرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا فَيُضَاعِفَهُ لَهُ أَضْعَافًا كَثِيرَةً ۚ

52
00:03:53,179 --> 00:03:58,655
وَاللَّهُ يَقْبِضُ وَيَبْسُطُ وَإِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ۞

53
00:04:00,544 --> 00:04:10,004
فَهَزَمُوهُمْ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَقَتَلَ دَاوُودُ جَالُوتَ وَآتَاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ

54
00:04:11,181 --> 00:04:19,643
 وَآتَاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَهُ مِمَّا يَشَاءُ ۗ

55
00:04:20,437 --> 00:04:27,795
وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ اللَّهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لَفَسَدَتِ الْأَرْضُ

56
00:04:27,872 --> 00:04:33,090
 وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ۞

57
00:04:34,062 --> 00:04:38,606
And if it were not for Allah checking some people by means of others,

58
00:04:39,183 --> 00:04:40,959
the Earth would have been corrupted,

59
00:04:41,554 --> 00:04:43,537
but Allah is full of bounty to the worlds.

60
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:48,619
Al-Imam Al-Halimi(ألإمام ألحليمي), in his book Sho'ba-Al-Iman(شعبة الإيمان),

61
00:04:48,643 --> 00:04:50,167
he comments on this Ayah(آية), he says:

62
00:04:52,151 --> 00:04:57,786
Allah clarified that if it weren't for Allah checking the non-believers through the believers,

63
00:04:58,716 --> 00:05:01,414
and giving the believers authority to protect Islam,

64
00:05:02,018 --> 00:05:03,976
and break the armies of disbelief,

65
00:05:04,410 --> 00:05:06,520
disbelief would have rained on earth,

66
00:05:07,282 --> 00:05:09,602
and the true religion would have been eliminated.

67
00:05:10,424 --> 00:05:15,032
This proves that the reason for the survival of religion is Jihad(جهاد)

68
00:05:15,715 --> 00:05:19,127
and whatever is in the status deserves to be a pillar of Eeman(ايمان).

69
00:05:20,207 --> 00:05:25,207
So he says that the reason why Islam survives is through Al-Jihad(ألجهاد).

70
00:05:27,314 --> 00:05:29,567
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says in Surah At-Touba(سورة التوبة) verse 5:

71
00:05:29,893 --> 00:05:37,881
فَإِذَا انسَلَخَ الأَشهُرُ الحُرُمُ فَاقتُلُوا المُشرِكينَ حَيثُ وَجَدتُموهُم

72
00:05:38,132 --> 00:05:43,762
وَخُذوهُم وَاحصُروهُم وَاقعُدوا لَهُم كُلَّ مَرصَدٍ ۚ

73
00:05:44,147 --> 00:05:52,055
فَإِن تابوا وَأَقامُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتَوُا الزَّكاةَ فَخَلّوا سَبيلَهُم ۚ

74
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:56,384
إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفورٌ رَحيمٌ۞

75
00:05:57,463 --> 00:06:00,599
Then kill the polytheists wherever you find them

76
00:06:00,654 --> 00:06:04,050
and capture them and besiege them and sit in wait for them

77
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:05,532
at every place of ambush.

78
00:06:07,398 --> 00:06:08,889
So this is about the Al-Mushrikeen(ألمشركين),

79
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:11,913
about Ahl-Al-Kitab(أهل الكتاب), Al-Touba(ألتوبة) Verse 29.

80
00:06:12,373 --> 00:06:20,734
قاتِلُوا الَّذينَ لا يُؤمِنونَ بِاللَّهِ وَلا بِاليَومِ الآخِرِ وَلا

81
00:06:21,212 --> 00:06:33,515
وَلا يُحَرِّمونَ ما حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ وَرَسولُهُ وَلا يَدينونَ دينَ الحَقِّ مِنَ الَّذينَ أوتُوا الكِتابَ حَتّىٰ

82
00:06:33,928 --> 00:06:40,965
 حَتّىٰ يُعطُوا الجِزيَةَ عَن يَدٍ وَهُم صاغِرونَ۞

83
00:06:43,147 --> 00:06:46,464
Fight those, who do not believe in Allah or in the last day

84
00:06:47,011 --> 00:06:51,630
and who do not consider unlawful what Allah and His Messenger made unlawful

85
00:06:52,331 --> 00:06:56,784
and who did not adopt the religion of truth from those who are given the Scripture,

86
00:06:57,038 --> 00:06:58,034
 the Christian and the Jews.

87
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:03,256
Fight until they give Jizya(جِزية) willingly, while they are humbled.

88
00:07:05,177 --> 00:07:10,068
So these are the Ayaat(آيات) that Al-Imam Ibn Nuhas(ألإمام إبن نُحاس) opens the chapter with.

89
00:07:11,655 --> 00:07:12,838
The Ahadith(احاديث)

90
00:07:15,973 --> 00:07:19,108
on the authority of Ibn e Umar رضي الله عنه,

91
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:22,503
The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

92
00:07:24,116 --> 00:07:26,717
I have been ordered to fight against the people,

93
00:07:27,408 --> 00:07:31,971
until they testify that there is none worthy of worship except Allah.

94
00:07:32,921 --> 00:07:35,190
And that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah,

95
00:07:36,484 --> 00:07:38,884
to establish prayer and give the Zaka'at(زكوة),

96
00:07:39,967 --> 00:07:44,717
then if they do that, their blood and wealth will be protected from me,

97
00:07:45,281 --> 00:07:47,614
except in accordance with the right of Islam.

98
00:07:48,527 --> 00:07:51,110
And the reckoning will be with Allah the Exalted.

99
00:07:52,448 --> 00:07:57,235
This Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ), Muslim(مُسلم), At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Nasai(نَسائ), Abu Daud(أبوداؤد),

100
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:59,958
Ibn Majah(إبن ماجه), Ahmad(أحمد) Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي), Ibn e Habban(إبن حبَّان),

101
00:08:00,299 --> 00:08:02,617
Ad-Dar Butni(ألدار بطني) and Imam Malik(إمام مالك),

102
00:08:03,189 --> 00:08:06,587
and it was narrated by Ibn e Umar(إبن عمر), Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره), Jabir Ibn Abdullah(جابرإبن عبدالله),

103
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:08,641
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك), Jarir Ibn Abdullah(جرير إبن عبدالله),

104
00:08:09,089 --> 00:08:11,993
Aus Ibn Abi Aus(أوس بن أبي أوس), Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس), Sahal Ibn Saad(سهل بن سعد),

105
00:08:12,156 --> 00:08:15,207
An-Nauman Bin Bashir(ألنعمان إبن بشير), Baraka Bin Ashab(باركة بن أشيب),

106
00:08:15,556 --> 00:08:18,748
Abu Bakara(أبوبكرة), Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذإبن جبل) and Samura Bin Jundab(سمرة بن جندب).

107
00:08:19,372 --> 00:08:24,259
So, the Hadith(حديث) is beyond any doubt?

108
00:08:25,371 --> 00:08:27,895
It is the highest level of Hadith(حديث), it is Mutawatir(متواتر).

109
00:08:29,385 --> 00:08:36,441
The Hadith(حديث) says that I've been commanded to fight against the people,

110
00:08:36,481 --> 00:08:41,474
until they testify that there's not worthy of worship than Allah and Salah(صلاة) and Zaka'at(زكوة).

111
00:08:42,314 --> 00:08:45,907
How do you reconcile between this Hadith(حديث). And the Ayah(آية);

112
00:08:45,955 --> 00:08:46,891
لا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ

113
00:08:48,217 --> 00:08:49,446
There is no compulsion in religion.

114
00:08:49,915 --> 00:08:50,716
 And the other Ayah(آية):

115
00:08:50,725 --> 00:08:52,724
أَفَأَنتَ تُكْرِهُ ٱلنَّاسَ حَتَّىٰ يَكُونُواْ مُؤْمِنِينَ

116
00:08:53,228 --> 00:08:56,045
Can you force the people to become believers?

117
00:08:56,529 --> 00:08:58,808
 How do you reconcile between the Ayah(آية) and Hadith(حديث)?

118
00:09:01,468 --> 00:09:02,411
How do you bring the two together?

119
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:05,796
The Ayah(آية) says: Fight them! Until they say:

120
00:09:05,864 --> 00:09:06,641
لا اله إلَّا الله

121
00:09:08,698 --> 00:09:09,528
What do you do?

122
00:09:12,346 --> 00:09:12,949
Any point?

123
00:09:16,552 --> 00:09:21,289
Now Ibn e Hajr(إبن حجر), he mentions a few different opinions on this.

124
00:09:23,012 --> 00:09:24,052
And he says:

125
00:09:27,664 --> 00:09:31,824
The people are fought to establish the dominance of Allah's law.

126
00:09:32,982 --> 00:09:35,087
This objective can be met through many means,

127
00:09:35,753 --> 00:09:37,405
it could be met by fighting them,

128
00:09:37,898 --> 00:09:41,408
it can also be met by them accepting the law of Allah and paying Jizya(جِزية).

129
00:09:42,178 --> 00:09:46,639
It can also be met by some sort of peace accord between the Muslims and others,

130
00:09:47,050 --> 00:09:50,518
in which the non Muslims will not oppose the words of Allah in anyway.

131
00:09:51,753 --> 00:09:56,748
 So the Ayah(آية), that means that the people either become Muslim,

132
00:09:57,272 --> 00:09:59,819
 or they accept the law of Allah and its dominance over the land.

133
00:10:01,215 --> 00:10:05,736
So Ahl e Zima(أهل الذمة) are non Muslims, who have accepted the dominance of  law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

134
00:10:05,875 --> 00:10:07,198
and they pay the Jizya(جِزية)

135
00:10:07,589 --> 00:10:13,323
 to signify the fact that they have accepted the dominance of the law of Allah over them.

136
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:15,572
Therefore, there's no contradiction.

137
00:10:17,916 --> 00:10:19,792
So people are not forced individually

138
00:10:19,877 --> 00:10:22,595
because you cannot force something down the hearts of somebody else.

139
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:28,049
However, the land belongs to Allah and it will be inherited by Al-Muttaqeen(ألمتقين).

140
00:10:29,402 --> 00:10:32,068
The next Hadith(حديث) is narrated by Al-Hakim(ألحاكم)

141
00:10:32,108 --> 00:10:33,282
 and it is Sahih(صحيح),

142
00:10:35,291 --> 00:10:40,289
Abu Musanna Al Abdi(أبومثنى ألعبدي) said: I heard Abul Khasasia(أبوالخصاصية) say:

143
00:10:40,450 --> 00:10:44,856
I came to the Messenger of Allah and said: I would pledged allegiance to him,

144
00:10:45,339 --> 00:10:49,069
Abul Khasasia(أبوالخصاصية), he wanted to give Rasool Allah ﷺ, the Baiyah(بَيْعة) of Islam.

145
00:10:51,206 --> 00:10:56,866
The Messenger of Allah took the pledge from me to testify that there is none worthy of worship other than Allah,

146
00:10:58,128 --> 00:11:00,084
that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah,

147
00:11:00,969 --> 00:11:02,569
to pray the five prayers,

148
00:11:03,077 --> 00:11:04,215
to fast Ramadan(رمضان),

149
00:11:04,529 --> 00:11:05,446
to pay Zakat(زكواة)

150
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:08,513
to make Hajj(حَجْ) and to fight in the sake of Allah.

151
00:11:10,195 --> 00:11:13,492
Now Abul Khasasia(أبوالخصاصية), being a very honest man,

152
00:11:14,239 --> 00:11:20,622
he said: O Rasool Ullah, two have those I cannot commit to, :

153
00:11:22,823 --> 00:11:25,895
very frank! He said: I want to give you Baiyah(بَيْعة) of Islam.

154
00:11:26,014 --> 00:11:27,761
Rasool Ullah told him: These are the terms,

155
00:11:27,911 --> 00:11:30,343
he said: I have exception to two of them.

156
00:11:30,628 --> 00:11:31,393
He said:

157
00:11:32,556 --> 00:11:35,029
The first is Zaka'at(زكوة), I only have 10 camels.

158
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:37,236
they constitute my entire wealth.

159
00:11:38,481 --> 00:11:39,565
 The second is Jihad(جهاد).

160
00:11:40,484 --> 00:11:45,663
I heard that whoever runs away from the battlefield has incurred the wrath of Allah.

161
00:11:46,283 --> 00:11:51,537
 I am afraid: If fighting faces me. I might fear death,  and my spirit would fail me.

162
00:11:54,149 --> 00:11:55,704
So his concern with Jihad(جهاد) is,

163
00:11:55,729 --> 00:12:00,165
 he was afraid that he might be committing a Kabira(كبيرة), major sins, if he runs away.

164
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:03,069
 So he said: I don't want to get myself into that.

165
00:12:03,572 --> 00:12:04,898
 Rasool Allah ﷺ told him,

166
00:12:06,214 --> 00:12:07,494
after he grabbed his hand

167
00:12:08,792 --> 00:12:11,967
لا صدقة ولا جهاد فبِمَا تدخل الجنة إذن

168
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:15,234
No Sadaqah(صدقة) and No Jihad(جهاد), and how will you enter paradise?

169
00:12:17,558 --> 00:12:20,449
No Sadaqah(صدقة) and No Jihad(جهاد), How can you enter into paradise?

170
00:12:21,214 --> 00:12:23,232
We need to all ask ourselves that question,

171
00:12:23,969 --> 00:12:25,351
taking Jannah(جنة) for granted.

172
00:12:26,311 --> 00:12:27,388
The third Hadith(حديث),

173
00:12:27,670 --> 00:12:30,451
 and this is narrated by Tabarani(طبراني) in Al-Kabir(ألكبير),

174
00:12:30,732 --> 00:12:32,384
Salamah Ibn Nufail(سلمة إبن نفيل) said:

175
00:12:33,273 --> 00:12:36,252
And I wanted you to pay very close attention to this Hadith(حديث), it's very important.

176
00:12:36,849 --> 00:12:42,847
Before I narrate the Hadith(حديث), Let me ask you this question.

177
00:12:46,034 --> 00:12:51,127
 Is Jihad(جهاد) is Ibadah(عبادة) that is intended in itself?

178
00:12:52,257 --> 00:12:56,977
 Or is the Jihad(جهاد) a Ibadah(عبادة) that means something else?

179
00:13:01,602 --> 00:13:06,675
 Is Jihad(جهاد) an Ibadah(عبادة) that is that is intended in itself? Or is it a means to an end?

180
00:13:07,911 --> 00:13:10,762
Is Jihad(جهاد) a means towards the end of the people to becoming Muslim?

181
00:13:10,896 --> 00:13:13,323
Or is it mean towards the end of Khilafah(خِلَافَه)?

182
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:15,959
Or is Jihad(جهاد) is  intended in its ownself?

183
00:13:17,953 --> 00:13:20,320
It's Ibadah(عبادة) in its own self. And what's the evidence for that?

184
00:13:21,494 --> 00:13:26,545
Because it can easily be argued that Jihad(جهاد) is a means to Khilafah(خِلَافَه) or means to Da'wah(دعوة).

185
00:13:27,171 --> 00:13:29,623
Which means that if it means something else, if people become Muslim,

186
00:13:29,711 --> 00:13:31,037
there's no point in Jihad(جهاد).

187
00:13:33,518 --> 00:13:35,391
So if we say that it's not a means in itself,

188
00:13:37,054 --> 00:13:40,530
then if we can invite people to Islam without Jihad(جهاد),

189
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,593
and they would embrace it, there is no need for Jihad(جهاد) then.

190
00:13:44,106 --> 00:13:48,925
So what’s the evidence of the fact that it's Ibadah(عبادة) in itself?

191
00:13:49,052 --> 00:13:50,855
Let's read this Hadith(حديث) and see.

192
00:13:54,449 --> 00:13:55,867
Because that's a very important argument.

193
00:13:55,967 --> 00:13:59,316
Yani(يعني), one can say: Why not just make Da'wah(دعوة), why do you have to fight the people?

194
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:03,988
If we can distribute brochures and we can have our stalls and books,

195
00:14:04,067 --> 00:14:05,952
Why do I have to fight people? What's the point?

196
00:14:10,209 --> 00:14:11,342
 Salamah Ibn Nufail(سلمة إبن نفيل) said:

197
00:14:12,349 --> 00:14:16,554
 While I was sitting with Rasool Ullah, a man came to him and said:

198
00:14:16,628 --> 00:14:19,968
O Messenger of Allah, horses are being discarded,

199
00:14:20,941 --> 00:14:22,559
 and weapons are being laid down.

200
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:25,704
And some people are claiming that there is no more fighting.

201
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:30,248
 This apparently happened after “Fath Makkah(فتح مكه)” victory was complete.

202
00:14:31,416 --> 00:14:34,831
Horses are discarded. We lay down our weapons.

203
00:14:35,078 --> 00:14:39,613
 Let's go back to our business take care of our farms. There's no more fighting. That's it.

204
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,440
إذَجاء نصرالله والفتح

205
00:14:44,262 --> 00:14:47,162
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ says? Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

206
00:14:47,209 --> 00:14:50,770
كذبو ألآن جاء القتال

207
00:14:51,423 --> 00:14:54,443
They are lying. Now fighting has just begun.

208
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:59,430
 And a party of my Ummah(امة) will fight for the sake of Allah.

209
00:15:00,979 --> 00:15:03,040
And those, who oppose them will not harm them.

210
00:15:04,646 --> 00:15:10,779
And Allah will deviate the hearts of some men to provide for that party from them, by fighting them.

211
00:15:12,032 --> 00:15:15,410
 And they will continue fighting until the final hour starts.

212
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:20,104
 And good will remain on the foreheads of horses, until the day of judgment.

213
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:24,548
And war will not end until Yajooj(ياجوج) and Majoj(ماجوج) come out.

214
00:15:26,815 --> 00:15:31,726
 There's a similar Hadith(حديث) narrated by Imam Nasai(إمام نسائ) and then we'll read the commentary on it.

215
00:15:33,676 --> 00:15:37,933
Salman Bin Nufail(سلمان بن نفيل) said: While I was sitting with Rasool Allah ﷺ, a man came to him and said:

216
00:15:38,233 --> 00:15:40,906
 O Messenger of Allah, horses are being humiliated,

217
00:15:41,502 --> 00:15:42,722
and weapons are being laid down

218
00:15:43,155 --> 00:15:45,736
and people are claiming there's no more Jihad(جهاد) and war has ended.

219
00:15:46,431 --> 00:15:51,685
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: They are lying, fighting has just begun, fighting has just begun.

220
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:55,095
And a party of my Ummah(امة) will remain fighting on the true path.

221
00:15:55,664 --> 00:16:00,574
 And Allah will deviate the hearts of some men and Allah will provide the fighters from them.

222
00:16:01,495 --> 00:16:04,334
Until the final hour starts and the promise of Allah is fulfilled.

223
00:16:05,123 --> 00:16:07,674
 Good is in the foreheads of horses until the day of judgment.

224
00:16:08,408 --> 00:16:12,098
It is been revealed to me that I will be departing you soon and you will follow me,

225
00:16:12,178 --> 00:16:16,527
 while you are fighting each other, and the house of the believers is in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

226
00:16:17,508 --> 00:16:23,249
Now what does As-Sindi(السندي) saying in his commentary on Sunnan Nasai(سنن نسائ), he says:

227
00:16:24,443 --> 00:16:30,879
Humiliating horses means ignoring them and belittling their importance were not using them for combat

228
00:16:33,118 --> 00:16:37,567
and he comments on the statement now fighting has started, now fighting has started. He said:

229
00:16:38,857 --> 00:16:42,171
 The repetition is to reveal the importance of the message.

230
00:16:42,922 --> 00:16:48,407
 And it means that fighting is only increasing and that Allah has just prescribed it.

231
00:16:48,706 --> 00:16:55,172
 So how can it end so soon, or it means that the real fighting has just begun.

232
00:16:55,497 --> 00:16:59,214
Because so far they have been fighting only within their territory, the land of the Arabs.

233
00:16:59,791 --> 00:17:03,118
 But now it's time for them to carry the battle to further lands.

234
00:17:03,845 --> 00:17:08,468
It's actually, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر), who carried out the Jihad(جهاد) outside of the Arabian Peninsula.

235
00:17:09,257 --> 00:17:12,939
 And that was the golden era of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

236
00:17:13,773 --> 00:17:17,292
The Muslims in that time were fighting more, than in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

237
00:17:17,374 --> 00:17:19,743
They have opened fronts all over.

238
00:17:21,267 --> 00:17:24,480
By the way, these comments by Sindi(سندي) I inserted, they are not in the book.

239
00:17:26,202 --> 00:17:28,201
But they're important for this Hadith(حديث).

240
00:17:29,439 --> 00:17:33,500
And then he says, and this is the important statement here, Allah will deviate the hearts of some.

241
00:17:34,739 --> 00:17:35,779
What does that mean?

242
00:17:36,728 --> 00:17:41,527
It means Allah will always provide this party of believers,  the Taifah(طائفة)

243
00:17:42,496 --> 00:17:48,026
 with men to fight, even if it means deviating their hearts from Eeman(ايمان) to Kuffr(كفر).

244
00:17:49,646 --> 00:17:52,754
Rasool Allah ﷺ saying: Let's assume that everybody becomes Muslim,

245
00:17:52,954 --> 00:17:55,503
Allah will take some people and deviate their hearts,

246
00:17:56,013 --> 00:17:57,803
 so that the Ibadah(عبادة) of Jihad(جهاد) is not stopped.

247
00:17:59,259 --> 00:18:02,908
Therefore it is intended in its own self, it is Ibadah(عبادة) in its own self,

248
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:04,485
it’s not mean to something else.

249
00:18:08,647 --> 00:18:13,131
 That is to bless these believers by providing them with the honor of fighting  in His sake

250
00:18:13,334 --> 00:18:15,154
 and the ultimate pleasure of pleasing Allah.

251
00:18:16,274 --> 00:18:21,145
 In other words,Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will never deprive the Ummah(امة) of the opportunity of fighting Jihad(جهاد),

252
00:18:21,709 --> 00:18:22,739
the opportunity will always be there,

253
00:18:22,775 --> 00:18:26,140
it's just a matter of who will accept the invitation and who will turn it down.

254
00:18:28,144 --> 00:18:30,996
So this is a critical Hadith(حديث) in this argument because it says that

255
00:18:31,996 --> 00:18:34,384
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ want this Ibadah(عبادة) to follow,

256
00:18:34,729 --> 00:18:38,441
and Allah wants to honor this Taifah(طائفة), and Allah wants to give them the Ajr(أجْر),

257
00:18:38,711 --> 00:18:41,329
 therefore Allah will always create for them their targets.

258
00:18:42,182 --> 00:18:43,562
The targets will always be there,

259
00:18:43,904 --> 00:18:47,605
so that this Taifah(طائفة) can carry on with their Ibadah(عبادة) of Jihad Fee Sabil-Lillah(في سبيل الله)

260
00:18:54,305 --> 00:19:00,052
Now when it says that Allah will deviate the hearts of some, so that Allah will give them Rizq(رزق) through them.

261
00:19:01,499 --> 00:19:05,962
 It could either mean, so that Allah will give them Rizq(رزق) of Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

262
00:19:06,811 --> 00:19:10,725
 Allah will give them  the Rizq(رزق) of Ajr(أجْر) or Allah will give them the Rizq(رزق) of Ghanimah(غنيمه).

263
00:19:12,623 --> 00:19:14,790
It mean all of the above.

264
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:23,975
And you know one has the right to ask.

265
00:19:27,302 --> 00:19:34,406
 We hear all of the Ahadith(احاديث) about small details in the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ, about small issues.

266
00:19:35,248 --> 00:19:40,365
We hear them all over the Masajid(مساجد) and Ahadith(احاديث) like this are hidden from the public,

267
00:19:41,479 --> 00:19:43,899
 When they are very critical and important Ahadith(احاديث).

268
00:19:43,968 --> 00:19:47,748
How come these Ahadith(احاديث) are not presented and told to the people.

269
00:19:48,278 --> 00:19:54,221
 There's an attempt by Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) to block out some aspects of the religion.

270
00:20:00,036 --> 00:20:00,740
Number five;

271
00:20:02,492 --> 00:20:05,356
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) narrates that Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

272
00:20:06,028 --> 00:20:10,128
 Fight the non believers with your wealth, arms and tongues.

273
00:20:11,377 --> 00:20:16,591
جاهدالمشركين بأموالكم وايديكم والسنتكم

274
00:20:18,484 --> 00:20:25,611
With your wealth is clear, and usually wealth comes before the physical fighting.

275
00:20:27,264 --> 00:20:31,548
And that tells you something and then tongues.

276
00:20:31,611 --> 00:20:32,822
What does tongues mean?

277
00:20:32,870 --> 00:20:33,732
 Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

278
00:20:34,811 --> 00:20:40,798
With your tongue means, hurt the non-believers by letting them hear what displeases them.

279
00:20:42,213 --> 00:20:47,543
And this Hadith(حديث) is Sahih(صحيح) it's in An-Nasae(ألنسائ), Abu Daud(ابوداؤد), Ahmad(أحمد) and Al-Hakim(ألحاكم).

280
00:20:49,979 --> 00:20:51,556
Hadith(حديث) number six.

281
00:20:53,312 --> 00:20:56,760
The Messenger of Allah said I have five commands for you;

282
00:20:57,348 --> 00:21:03,979
To listen, to obey, to fight Jihad(جهاد), to make Hijrah(هجرة) and to stay with Jamaah(جماعة).

283
00:21:04,714 --> 00:21:06,145
 These are my five commands to you.

284
00:21:06,950 --> 00:21:09,938
And this in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Ahmad(أحمد) and Abdul Razzaq(عبدالرزاق) and it is Hasan(حسن).

285
00:21:13,955 --> 00:21:19,199
Number Seven, Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس)  narrates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

286
00:21:21,364 --> 00:21:25,464
There is no Hijrah(هجرة) after the opening of Makkah.

287
00:21:26,219 --> 00:21:28,139
But there is Jihad(جهاد) and intention.

288
00:21:29,166 --> 00:21:31,515
And if you are called to fight then fight.

289
00:21:32,731 --> 00:21:35,082
This Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم).

290
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:37,877
 Let's talk about the Ayah(آية),

291
00:21:39,167 --> 00:21:48,612
ٱنفِرُواْ خِفَافًا وَثِقَالًا وَجَٰهِدُواْ بِأَمْوَٰلِكُمْ وَأَنفُسِكُمْ فِى سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ۚ

292
00:21:49,748 --> 00:21:52,563
 ذَٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ۝

293
00:21:55,648 --> 00:21:58,720
What does that Khifafah(خفافًا) and Siqala(ثقالا) mean, the translation of the Ayah(آية):

294
00:21:58,776 --> 00:22:00,742
 Go forth whether light or heavy

295
00:22:01,242 --> 00:22:06,210
and strive with your wealth and your lives and the cause of Allah that's better for you if you only knew.

296
00:22:06,578 --> 00:22:08,059
 What does light and heavy mean?

297
00:22:09,438 --> 00:22:10,770
 What is light and heavy mean?

298
00:22:12,472 --> 00:22:17,402
One meaning is young and old.

299
00:22:18,934 --> 00:22:22,577
Qatadah(قتادة) says active or inactive, energetic or not.

300
00:22:24,914 --> 00:22:31,043
It is narrated that Abu Ayub رضي الله عنه, Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari(أبوأيوب ألأنصاري), he took rest from Jihad(جهاد) for a year.

301
00:22:32,796 --> 00:22:35,001
But then when he recited this Ayah(آية), he said:

302
00:22:35,249 --> 00:22:37,974
 I do not find for myself an excuse in this Ayah(آية).

303
00:22:40,998 --> 00:22:44,351
So he resumed his Jihad(جهاد), now keep in mind then Jihad(جهاد) of what?

304
00:22:44,576 --> 00:22:47,105
Jihad At-Talab(جهادألطلب), it wasn't Jihad Ad-Dafah(جهادألدفعة), it was offensive,

305
00:22:47,791 --> 00:22:49,023
and it was fardh e Kafaya(فرض كفاية).

306
00:22:51,944 --> 00:22:56,358
 Abu Shayba(أبوشعيبة)  narrated with an authentic narration to Al-Hakim(ألحاكم), He said:

307
00:22:57,221 --> 00:22:58,970
Busy or preoccupied,

308
00:22:59,682 --> 00:23:01,932
 light and heavy means busy or preoccupied.

309
00:23:03,777 --> 00:23:07,486
It is also said: The heavy is the one, who has property which he fears

310
00:23:08,137 --> 00:23:09,720
 would be lost if he joins Jihad(جهاد),

311
00:23:10,037 --> 00:23:12,714
while the light is the one, who has no property to worry about.

312
00:23:14,756 --> 00:23:18,219
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says: The Ayah(آية) is general and applies to everyone

313
00:23:18,301 --> 00:23:20,220
 whether joining is easy for them or not.

314
00:23:21,321 --> 00:23:26,192
Az-Zuhri(أظهري) states that Ibn-e-Musayib(إبن مسيَّب) joined the army when he had already lost one of his eyes due to old age.

315
00:23:27,975 --> 00:23:29,013
 He was told, you are ill,

316
00:23:29,273 --> 00:23:30,548
he said: Astagfirullah(أستغفرالله),

317
00:23:31,416 --> 00:23:33,106
Allah says: The light and heavy.

318
00:23:33,672 --> 00:23:39,508
If I am incapable of fighting, at least I will increase the number of the army and will guard your luggage.

319
00:23:40,667 --> 00:23:44,083
 It's Saeed Bin Musaiyib(سعيد بن مسيَّب), a Tabaee(تابعي), is saying even if I can't fight,

320
00:23:44,596 --> 00:23:46,872
I'm going to go with you and guard your luggage.

321
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:55,791
It's amazing how some people try to find every argument to run away from fighting.

322
00:23:56,430 --> 00:24:00,197
While some people try to find every argument to join the fighting.

323
00:24:08,215 --> 00:24:10,698
Abu Ya'la(أبويعلى) and Al-Hakim(ألحاكم) narrate, with an authentic chain.

324
00:24:11,590 --> 00:24:14,782
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) said that Abu Talha(أبوطلحة) recited At-Tauba(ألتوبة)

325
00:24:14,804 --> 00:24:17,135
and when he passed by verse, Go forth light or heavy.

326
00:24:17,859 --> 00:24:21,492
And he said: I see that Allah is calling upon me whether I'm young or old.

327
00:24:22,604 --> 00:24:24,580
So he told his sons to prepare him for combat.

328
00:24:25,145 --> 00:24:28,058
They said: You have already fought with the Rasool Allah ﷺ, until he died.

329
00:24:28,455 --> 00:24:30,392
And then you fought with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) until he died.

330
00:24:30,791 --> 00:24:32,740
And then you fought with Umar(عُمَر), until he died.

331
00:24:33,335 --> 00:24:36,822
So now let us fight on your behalf, let us do the fighting.

332
00:24:37,508 --> 00:24:40,274
He said: Prepare me for combat.

333
00:24:40,925 --> 00:24:47,161
So they did and he went on an exhibition in the sea and he died.

334
00:24:47,716 --> 00:24:50,905
Now they didn't find an Island to bury him, until seven days later.

335
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:52,258
 But his body never changed.

336
00:24:57,496 --> 00:25:01,875
Abdul Razzaq(عبدالرزاق) says that Manhool(منحول), Manhool(منحول) is one of At-Tabieen(تابعين).

337
00:25:04,197 --> 00:25:05,768
 Manhool(منحول) is to face Al-Qibla(ألقبله).

338
00:25:07,358 --> 00:25:09,808
And he would make an oath in the name Allah, he would say:

339
00:25:11,104 --> 00:25:15,728
In the name of Allah going out in Ghazoo(غزؤ) is mandatory on you.

340
00:25:16,951 --> 00:25:20,497
 And then he make that oath the second time, a third time, he would make the 10 times

341
00:25:21,075 --> 00:25:24,010
and then he would tell anyone, everybody around him. Do you want to make it more?

342
00:25:24,917 --> 00:25:26,833
 Do you want me to make this oath more than 10 times.

343
00:25:27,357 --> 00:25:29,844
That going out in the Ghazoo(غزؤ) is mandatory on you.

344
00:25:35,874 --> 00:25:39,080
Tayeb(طيِّب) now, is Jihad(جهاد) Fardh Kifaya(فرض كِفاية) or Fardh Ain(فرض عين).

345
00:25:41,846 --> 00:25:44,798
Now I'll read what Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

346
00:25:46,593 --> 00:25:52,556
 Realize that attacking the non believers in their territories is a collective duty.

347
00:25:52,918 --> 00:25:55,532
 So now we're talking about attacking them in their land.

348
00:25:56,816 --> 00:26:01,349
Collective duty is Fardh Kifaya(فرض كِفاية), I am translating Fardh Kifaya(فرض كِفاية) as collective duty.

349
00:26:02,347 --> 00:26:10,223
Collective duty or Fardh Kifaya(فرض كِفاية) is something that is.... as long as some of the Ummah(امة) are doing it.

350
00:26:12,380 --> 00:26:16,036
Then that relieves the others from the responsibility.

351
00:26:21,506 --> 00:26:23,665
Fardh Ain(فرض عين) is something that everybody has to do.

352
00:26:24,645 --> 00:26:28,288
If I pray, I don't relief you from the responsibility of praying.

353
00:26:30,075 --> 00:26:34,957
 For the Fardh Kifaya(فرض كِفاية) for example, Yani(يعني) Al-Ghazali(ألغزالي) says:

354
00:26:35,001 --> 00:26:37,885
 If there's a Muslim village and there's no physician in that village,

355
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:42,151
then it's Fardh(فرض) for at least one of them, to fulfill that post.

356
00:26:43,232 --> 00:26:45,296
If they don't, then everybody's committing a sin.

357
00:26:46,277 --> 00:26:52,925
 But if they do appoint a physician, then everyone else is relieved, not everybody has to be a doctor,

358
00:26:53,823 --> 00:26:55,996
as long as somebody is doing it, that’s enough.

359
00:26:56,474 --> 00:26:58,548
 So it's the difference between Fardh Kifaya(فرض كِفاية) and Fardh Ain(فرض عين).

360
00:27:02,252 --> 00:27:09,364
So he says that attacking them in the territory is Fardh Kifaya(فرض كِفاية),  with the consensus of the scholars.

361
00:27:09,466 --> 00:27:12,336
 However, Ibn Ul-Musayib(إبن المسَّيب) and Ibn-e-Shuburma(إبن شبرمة),

362
00:27:12,637 --> 00:27:16,120
say that it is a duty Fardh Ain(فرض عين) on each and every individual.

363
00:27:16,717 --> 00:27:21,070
But this is a minority opinion, that attacking them in their land is Fardh Ain(فرض عين).

364
00:27:21,632 --> 00:27:24,746
And this is the opinion of Ibn Ul-Musayib(إبن المسَّيب) and Ibn-e-Shuburma(إبن شبرمة)

365
00:27:24,932 --> 00:27:28,577
 that everyone able to fight must go out in the Jihad At-Talab(جهاد الطلب)

366
00:27:28,756 --> 00:27:31,995
so it's Fardh Ain(فرض عين) on everybody, but again, this is a minority opinion.

367
00:27:34,586 --> 00:27:39,668
The minimum participation in Jihad(جهاد) is once a year, and more is always better.

368
00:27:40,765 --> 00:27:46,368
It is not allowed to have the year pass you by without any fighting, except out of necessity,

369
00:27:46,744 --> 00:27:50,389
 like the weakness of the Muslims, the great numbers of the enemy,

370
00:27:50,918 --> 00:27:56,597
fear of extermination if you attack them first, or lack of provisions or a similar excuse.

371
00:27:57,418 --> 00:28:00,604
So it needs to be done at least once a year.

372
00:28:01,948 --> 00:28:08,727
Otherwise, if there is no necessity, it is not allowed to delay attacking even unbelievers for more than a year.

373
00:28:08,925 --> 00:28:10,574
This is according to Imam Shafie(إمام ألشافعي),

374
00:28:12,941 --> 00:28:18,104
the Imam(اِمَام) of Al-Haramain(ألحرمين) says: I adopt the opinion of the scholars of Asool(أصول).

375
00:28:18,439 --> 00:28:22,411
 So the scholars of Fiqh(فقه) say that it's once year, the scholars of Asool(أصول) say:

376
00:28:23,024 --> 00:28:30,198
They stated that Jihad(جهاد) is a mandatory call, and must be established according to the ability,

377
00:28:30,894 --> 00:28:35,829
 until none remains in the world, but a Muslim, or one, who has admitted to Muslims.

378
00:28:37,041 --> 00:28:39,004
Thus Jihad(جهاد) is not limited to once a year.

379
00:28:39,781 --> 00:28:42,213
It should be done more frequently, if possible.

380
00:28:43,018 --> 00:28:46,842
 The opinion of the scholars of Fiqh(فقه) that Jihad(جهاد) is to be able to wage once a year

381
00:28:47,059 --> 00:28:53,355
is because usually the time spent in preparations for combat limit the ability to wage war more than once a year.

382
00:28:54,404 --> 00:29:00,031
 So this Yani(يعني) Imam(اِمَام) of Al-Haramain(ألحرمين) is saying:

383
00:29:00,909 --> 00:29:04,784
He's commenting on the opinion of the scholars of Fiqh(فقه) that should be done once a year.

384
00:29:05,015 --> 00:29:10,462
He says: The reason why the scholars of Fiqh(فقه) is limited once a year is because out of experience,

385
00:29:11,187 --> 00:29:13,375
 having more than one Ghazwa(غزوة) in a year is difficult.

386
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:19,996
You know the time to prepare for the Ghazwa(غزوة) makes it difficult to do it once a year.

387
00:29:21,057 --> 00:29:22,370
But Imam(اِمَام) of Al-Haramain(ألحرمين) says:

388
00:29:23,214 --> 00:29:27,067
 My opinion is that, it should be done more than that, if possible.

389
00:29:27,216 --> 00:29:30,146
And it's not limited to once a year. The only reason why it's limited to once a year

390
00:29:30,243 --> 00:29:31,679
is because of the circumstances.

391
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:36,773
Otherwise, it should be done, until the entire world has only a Muslim,

392
00:29:36,841 --> 00:29:39,160
or somebody who has submitted to Muslims.

393
00:29:40,602 --> 00:29:43,451
Otherwise, carry on as much as possible.

394
00:29:46,959 --> 00:29:50,279
 The author of the Mughni(مغني) from the Hanbali(حنبلي) school states,

395
00:29:51,349 --> 00:29:54,807
 the minimum Jihad(جهاد) is once a year.

396
00:29:55,552 --> 00:29:57,526
So it is mandatory every year.

397
00:29:58,126 --> 00:30:05,102
If there is a need to fight more, than once a year, it becomes mandatory on the Muslims to fulfill that need.

398
00:30:06,459 --> 00:30:08,168
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) states in his Tafsir(تفسير),

399
00:30:09,045 --> 00:30:14,893
it is mandatory on the Imam(اِمَام) to send an army of Muslims to the land of the enemy once every year.

400
00:30:15,715 --> 00:30:19,625
 And the Imam(اِمَام) should participate himself in such expeditions.

401
00:30:19,973 --> 00:30:26,389
Now, by the way, and the scholars of Andalus(أندلس) they're very deep when it comes to Jihad(جهاد),

402
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:28,600
because that was the land of Jihad(جهاد) for 800 years.

403
00:30:29,646 --> 00:30:33,560
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), they had some great Khulafaa(خلفاء) and Sultans.

404
00:30:34,130 --> 00:30:35,827
Like for example, Abdul Rahman As'salis(عبدالرحمن ألثالث),

405
00:30:36,725 --> 00:30:41,090
he used to make Jihad(جهاد) in winter once and in summer once,

406
00:30:42,940 --> 00:30:43,889
every year,

407
00:30:44,740 --> 00:30:46,311
And his reign was 50 years.

408
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:50,686
For 50 years he would made Jihad(جهاد) twice a year

409
00:30:51,263 --> 00:30:57,531
 and he continued leading the army himself for about 25 years, until he was unable.

410
00:30:59,028 --> 00:31:02,963
So Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) the Andalus(أندلس) was an amazing land because the Romans never give the Muslims a break.

411
00:31:03,745 --> 00:31:08,898
 And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) there's a narration.

412
00:31:11,474 --> 00:31:12,847
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

413
00:31:13,229 --> 00:31:16,450
فَارِسُ نَطْحَةٌ , أَوْ نَطْحَتَانِ ثُمَّ لَا فَارِسَ بَعْدَهَا أَبَدًا ,

414
00:31:17,380 --> 00:31:19,306
وَالرُّومُ ذَاتُ الْقُرُونِ

415
00:31:19,852 --> 00:31:22,792
كُلَّمَا هَلَكَ قَرْنٌ خَلَفَ مَكَانَهُ قَرْنٌ  ,

416
00:31:23,524 --> 00:31:25,746
,أَهْلُ صَخْرٍ وَأَهْلُ بَحْرٍ هَيْهَاتَ لِآخِرِ الدَّهْرِ

417
00:31:26,427 --> 00:31:29,556
هُمْ أَصْحَابُكُمْ مَا كَانَ فِي الْعَيْشِ خَيْرٌ

418
00:31:30,208 --> 00:31:31,448
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

419
00:31:31,524 --> 00:31:38,428
Persia is one butt or two butts,  you know what an animal butts.

420
00:31:39,708 --> 00:31:41,244
 So it's one knock or two knocks.

421
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:46,058
 And then there will be no more Persia after that, this once and twice,

422
00:31:48,856 --> 00:31:52,334
 Al-Qadsiyah(ألقادسية) and Nahwand(ألنهوند) and that was it.

423
00:31:54,065 --> 00:31:55,604
The Persian Empire ceased to exist.

424
00:31:56,258 --> 00:32:00,008
But then Rasool Allah ﷺ says, but Ar-Rome(ألروم) have many horns.

425
00:32:00,608 --> 00:32:04,052
Whenever you break a horn, another horn will grow in its place.

426
00:32:05,117 --> 00:32:08,159
 They are people of mountains and sea.

427
00:32:08,359 --> 00:32:14,259
In other words, they are capable of fighting inland, mountains, rocks, sea, wherever,

428
00:32:14,868 --> 00:32:18,474
Hayhata-hayhat(هيهات هيهات) they are going to be your companions.

429
00:32:18,934 --> 00:32:22,316
As long as there is good in living, this statement means.

430
00:32:22,696 --> 00:32:28,567
They are going to be your opponents and your enemy. As long as you're living on the face of the earth.

431
00:32:29,389 --> 00:32:32,968
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), that statement has proven true until this day.

432
00:32:34,321 --> 00:32:39,292
 The war between the Muslims and the Romans never ceased to exist and who are the Romans?

433
00:32:40,052 --> 00:32:43,511
When I say the Romans, I'm translating a Ar-Rome(ألروم) as Romans.

434
00:32:43,995 --> 00:32:53,797
But Ar-Rome(ألروم) in the Arabic sense means, the Arabs used to call the European people

435
00:32:54,956 --> 00:32:55,889
they would call them Ar-Rome(ألروم).

436
00:32:56,414 --> 00:33:01,259
So it's not limited to a political entity or geographical entity.

437
00:33:02,639 --> 00:33:09,825
 Ar-Rome(ألروم) for the Arabs is an ethnicity, it is the Europeans.

438
00:33:13,192 --> 00:33:18,362
Therefore, Europe and its extensions would fall under Ar-Rome(ألروم).

439
00:33:18,887 --> 00:33:27,588
When I say its extensions, US, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, these are all extensions of Europe.

440
00:33:28,626 --> 00:33:29,844
 Or they are Roman people.

441
00:33:32,429 --> 00:33:38,031
 The war started in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ Mu'ta(مؤته) and Tabook(تبوك).

442
00:33:38,774 --> 00:33:44,741
And it carried on in the time of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر), Uthman(عثمان), Ali(علي), Bannu Umayyah(بنوأميَّة),

443
00:33:45,530 --> 00:33:50,488
Bannu Abbas(بنوعباس), Al-Uthmaniyeen(ألعثمانيين), Al-Uthmaniyeen(ألعثمانيين) pretty much all what they were fighting,

444
00:33:50,594 --> 00:33:53,330
the only people, they were fighting against, is the Romans.

445
00:33:54,072 --> 00:33:58,506
Al-Andalus(ألأندلس) eight hundred years of constant Jihad(جهاد) against Ar-Rome(ألروم).

446
00:33:59,492 --> 00:34:02,473
And as we know from the Ahadith(احاديث) of fittan(فتن).

447
00:34:03,101 --> 00:34:06,202
The Malhama(ملحمة)  is between the Muslims and the Ar-Rome(ألروم).

448
00:34:06,739 --> 00:34:13,588
 So this is a very protected, long conflict that will continue until the day of judgment.

449
00:34:21,205 --> 00:34:24,314
So Al-Qurtabi(ألقرطبي) states in his Tafsir(تفسير), it is mandatory on the Imam(اِمَام)

450
00:34:24,339 --> 00:34:28,825
to send an army of Muslims to the land of the enemy, once every year and

451
00:34:29,066 --> 00:34:33,152
the Imam(اِمَام) should participate himself in such expeditions.

452
00:34:33,492 --> 00:34:35,836
If not, then he should send someone capable,

453
00:34:36,003 --> 00:34:40,734
 whom he trusts, to call them to Islam, to keep away their harm,

454
00:34:41,192 --> 00:34:45,318
and to give victory to the religion of Allah, until they enter Islam or pay Jizya(جِزية).

455
00:34:47,245 --> 00:34:52,205
Notice that Al-Qurtabi(ألقرطبي) states that one of the objectives of sending the armies is to keep away their harm?

456
00:34:52,993 --> 00:34:59,647
This is an indication that Muslims will never experience peace, unless Jihad(جهاد) is established,

457
00:35:00,414 --> 00:35:03,107
because the harm of the enemy can only be stopped through Jihad(جهاد)

458
00:35:03,882 --> 00:35:10,370
 no peaceful means will deliver that, to the Ummah(امة).

459
00:35:12,660 --> 00:35:16,445
So called roadmaps to success or roadmaps to hellfire.

460
00:35:23,924 --> 00:35:27,105
And these are the statements of Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس):

461
00:35:27,151 --> 00:35:29,430
Jihad(جهاد) is not mandatory on children,

462
00:35:30,157 --> 00:35:32,415
the mentally incapable women and the ill,

463
00:35:33,210 --> 00:35:37,869
 it is mandatory, however  on the one eye, the one who is suffering from a mild illness

464
00:35:38,056 --> 00:35:43,189
such as a headache, a sore tooth, or a fever, or the one who has a slight limp.

465
00:35:44,359 --> 00:35:46,023
 This is in the Mad'hab(مذهب) of Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

466
00:35:46,536 --> 00:35:50,131
 And I don't know of any disagreement regarding that and Allah knows best.

467
00:35:51,987 --> 00:35:57,969
It is the consensus of scholars that one cannot participate in Ghazoo(غزؤ), without the permission of parents.

468
00:35:58,786 --> 00:36:00,685
 And this is talking about Jihad-At-Talab(جهادالطلب), Ghazoo(غزؤ).

469
00:36:01,628 --> 00:36:04,752
This is all regarding the Jihad(جهاد), which is a collective duty,

470
00:36:05,397 --> 00:36:10,209
Fardh Kifaya(فرض كفاية), starting the non believers with war, and on their territory.

471
00:36:10,809 --> 00:36:15,707
But if the enemy enters the Muslim land, or even approaches it

472
00:36:15,932 --> 00:36:20,456
and amasses on its borders, even if they do not actually enter it,

473
00:36:21,563 --> 00:36:25,057
and their armies are double the size of that of the Muslims are less,

474
00:36:25,453 --> 00:36:28,370
than Jihad(جهاد) becomes mandatory on each and every individual.

475
00:36:29,348 --> 00:36:32,455
 Then the slave leaves without the permission of their master,

476
00:36:32,968 --> 00:36:34,984
 the woman without the permission her husband,

477
00:36:35,376 --> 00:36:38,374
if she has the strength to fight according to the stronger opinion,

478
00:36:38,897 --> 00:36:40,948
 the son without the permission of their parents,

479
00:36:41,350 --> 00:36:44,569
and the one in debt without the permission of the lender.

480
00:36:45,268 --> 00:36:53,375
So, in the case where it is the Jihad(جهاد) Fardh-Ain(فرض عين), there is no permission that is sought,

481
00:36:53,894 --> 00:36:59,189
all of the rules regarding permission of the wife and the husband, sons and the parents,

482
00:36:59,766 --> 00:37:05,245
slave from the owner, the one in the debt from the lender are abrogated.

483
00:37:05,777 --> 00:37:10,196
And also in that situation Jihad(جهاد) can be done individually,

484
00:37:10,246 --> 00:37:12,639
so it doesn't have to be done in Jam’aa(جماعة) or under an Ameer(أمير).

485
00:37:13,955 --> 00:37:20,224
If there is a Jam’aa(جماعة) or an Ameer(أمير) then it shouldn't be done with them, otherwise, the person is on their own.

486
00:37:21,452 --> 00:37:23,083
 That's when it's Fardh-Ain(فرض عين).

487
00:37:23,901 --> 00:37:25,439
When the Jihad(جهاد) becomes Fardh-Ain(فرض عين)?

488
00:37:26,070 --> 00:37:32,430
 Ibn ul Qadamah(إبن القدامة), Al-Maqdasi(ألمقدسي), gives three conditions when Jihad(جهاد) becomes Fardh-Ain(فرض عين).

489
00:37:32,852 --> 00:37:35,499
Number one, when the enemy attacks your land.

490
00:37:35,804 --> 00:37:39,469
 Number two, when the Imam(اِمَام) calls you out for Jihad(جهاد),

491
00:37:39,975 --> 00:37:41,923
and number three, when the Armies meet.

492
00:37:43,964 --> 00:37:47,926
 So if it is a voluntary Jihad(جهاد), and you're volunteer to go out,

493
00:37:49,073 --> 00:37:52,410
and then the army meets, you can't change your mind.

494
00:37:53,367 --> 00:37:57,172
Because then becomes Tawalini Zahaf(تولني ضحف) it becomes turning your back.

495
00:37:57,988 --> 00:37:58,986
 And it's one of the Kabair(كبائر).

496
00:37:59,856 --> 00:38:03,335
You didn't want to join, you shouldn't have join in the first place, when the Armies meet.

497
00:38:04,103 --> 00:38:05,651
It's too late to bail out, it becomes Fardh-Ain(فرض عين).

498
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:23,867
Tayeb(طيِّب), all of the above stated is the opinion of Imam Malik(إمام مالك), Ahmad(أحمد) and Abu Hanifah(ابوحنيفة).

499
00:38:24,183 --> 00:38:28,918
 In addition to the Mad'hab(مذهب) of the author of Shafie(شافعي), so that's the consensus of the four.

500
00:38:30,044 --> 00:38:35,133
And he says, they don't even have to attack your land, as long as the armies are getting ready.

501
00:38:37,249 --> 00:38:39,775
 Close to your border, it becomes Fardh-Ain(فرض عين).

502
00:38:42,527 --> 00:38:45,572
 If the enemy ambushes the Muslims in a certain area,

503
00:38:45,767 --> 00:38:49,211
and they don't have a chance to assemble together and prepare to fight,

504
00:38:49,712 --> 00:38:53,447
then whoever is faced by a non believer or group of non believers,

505
00:38:54,347 --> 00:38:58,596
 and the Muslim knows that if he surrenders he would be killed, then he must fight.

506
00:38:59,801 --> 00:39:01,069
So you're not allowed to surrender.

507
00:39:02,258 --> 00:39:07,484
There is no difference in this ruling between a free man, slave, man, woman, blind, lamp or ill.

508
00:39:08,461 --> 00:39:13,389
If there's a chance of survival, if the Muslim, if the person surrenders,

509
00:39:13,887 --> 00:39:16,943
 but would definitely be killed if he refuses to surrender

510
00:39:17,345 --> 00:39:20,770
then it is allowed to either surrender or fight, but fighting is better.

511
00:39:21,643 --> 00:39:26,535
 Again, if there is a chance of survival if the person surrenders,

512
00:39:27,247 --> 00:39:30,309
so they might just take you as a prisoner of war and not kill you.

513
00:39:31,654 --> 00:39:34,507
However, you will definitely be killed if you're fighting,

514
00:39:35,332 --> 00:39:37,457
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says: It's still better to fight.

515
00:39:40,748 --> 00:39:45,257
 If a woman thinks if she is taken prisoner, she would be sexually abused.

516
00:39:46,345 --> 00:39:51,025
 It is mandatory on her to fight, even if that would lead to her death.

517
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:58,660
Because if a person is forced to commit adultery or fornication, it is not allowed to give in,  even if to save one's life.

518
00:40:01,118 --> 00:40:06,729
 So the woman would rather die, fight and die than commit Zina(زنا).

519
00:40:09,965 --> 00:40:14,808
 Now if some Muslims in the attacked area, go to fight the enemy.

520
00:40:15,738 --> 00:40:22,274
And they are sufficient in numbers and are capable of fighting the enemy alone.

521
00:40:23,103 --> 00:40:30,715
 It is still a duty on the rest for help. So let's say that the enemy attacks,  Falastine(فلسطين).

522
00:40:33,531 --> 00:40:38,449
 And there is an army that was formed and this army can take on the enemy.

523
00:40:41,203 --> 00:40:45,628
It is still fardh(فرض) on the rest, didn't join to join, even though the army is sufficient.

524
00:40:46,558 --> 00:40:50,368
Why? Because now it's not Fardh-Kifaya(فرض كفاية), it's Fardh-Ain(فرض عين) on everyone.

525
00:40:52,143 --> 00:40:56,025
So you only go with a sufficient number, when it is attacking the enemy.

526
00:40:56,546 --> 00:41:00,714
But when the enemy attacks, even if a sufficient army is formed,

527
00:41:00,997 --> 00:41:04,959
it is still Fardh-Ain(فرض عين) on every and each single one to join in.

528
00:41:08,890 --> 00:41:13,247
If non believers descend on an unpopulated Muslim land

529
00:41:13,611 --> 00:41:17,548
that is far away from populated areas, there are two opinions in that.

530
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:21,121
And Al-Ghazali(ألغزالي) narrates both, the old Ghazali(غزالي).

531
00:41:21,645 --> 00:41:25,020
The first is that of Al-Imam Al-Harmain(إمام ألحرمين), he states

532
00:41:25,637 --> 00:41:28,187
that it does not become mandatory on Muslims to fight

533
00:41:28,234 --> 00:41:32,308
and put their lives in danger to protect such a secluded and unpopulated land.

534
00:41:33,669 --> 00:41:38,636
So, you don't have to fight them because it’s Fardh-Kifaya(فرض كفاية), it's not mandatory.

535
00:41:40,411 --> 00:41:43,627
The other opinion, which is the official position of the Mad'hab(مذهب)

536
00:41:44,062 --> 00:41:46,932
is that it is mandatory for Muslims to fight for that land.

537
00:41:48,051 --> 00:41:53,731
Al-Imam An-Nawawi(إمام أنَّووي) says that the opinion of Al-Imam Al-Harmain(إمام ألحرمين) and Juwairi(جويري) is unacceptable.

538
00:41:54,993 --> 00:41:56,300
 Al-Imam An-Nawawi(إمام أنَّووي) says:

