The only one who was coming forth it was Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان),

714
00:57:18,276 --> 00:57:22,978
Rasool Ullah is asking for donations nobody comes up, Uthman(عثمان) brings long line of horses,

715
00:57:25,014 --> 00:57:27,484
 asking for more, and nobody comes up and Uthman(عثمان) brings camels,

716
00:57:28,118 --> 00:57:29,998
asking for more Uthman(عثمان) goes back home.

717
00:57:30,311 --> 00:57:32,576
Every time he thinks that what he brings will be enough but it's not,

718
00:57:33,904 --> 00:57:39,261
 then he goes back home brings a big sack of silver coins, gives it to Rasool Ullah ﷺ Dirham(درهم).

719
00:57:40,319 --> 00:57:44,890
 Rasool Ullah is still asking for more, Uthman(عثمان) goes back home and brings a sack of Dinar(دينار) gold coins,

720
00:57:45,695 --> 00:57:48,100
and he pours it on the lap of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

721
00:57:49,100 --> 00:57:52,650
Rasool Allah ﷺ tosses the coins in his hand and he says,

722
00:57:53,144 --> 00:57:55,065
ما ضَرَّ عثمان ما عمل بعد اليوم

723
00:57:55,883 --> 00:57:58,653
Whatever Uthman(عثمان) does after this day, won’t harm him.

724
00:57:59,372 --> 00:58:01,327
He is guaranteed Jannah(جنة) because of what, he did.

725
00:58:01,914 --> 00:58:03,012
He could do whatever you wants.

726
00:58:05,016 --> 00:58:09,505
But the thing is it drained the treasury of the Muslim state.

727
00:58:10,006 --> 00:58:13,436
 War is a very expensive endeavor.

728
00:58:15,761 --> 00:58:21,457
Nevertheless, the irony is, the more Jihad(جهاد) that Muslims fight the wealthier they become.

729
00:58:24,895 --> 00:58:27,203
And it's an exponential curve, it just goes up.

730
00:58:29,761 --> 00:58:37,233
 Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was approached by Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة),

731
00:58:38,378 --> 00:58:41,602
who was one of his generals and the war against Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

732
00:58:44,007 --> 00:58:48,214
 Sharhabil(شرحبيل) came to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and He said: When he was Khalifah(خليفه),

733
00:58:48,273 --> 00:58:52,657
 are you contemplating Ghazoo(غزؤ) of Ar-Rome(ألروم)?

734
00:58:53,866 --> 00:58:55,440
Are you thinking about attacking the Romans.

735
00:58:56,749 --> 00:58:57,581
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Yes!

736
00:58:57,621 --> 00:59:01,861
And who told you about that because I was thinking about and I never disclosed that to anyone.

737
00:59:03,497 --> 00:59:06,382
 and it didn't really make sense because the Muslims were busy fighting in Persia.

738
00:59:07,145 --> 00:59:10,812
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was opening one town after another in Iraq,

739
00:59:12,096 --> 00:59:14,316
and it doesn't make sense to open up a new front with the Romans,

740
00:59:16,427 --> 00:59:18,254
 Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Why ? Tell me how come you know?

741
00:59:19,297 --> 00:59:21,317
Sharhabil Bin Hasana(شرحبيل بن حسنة) said: I saw a dream,

742
00:59:23,073 --> 00:59:30,121
I saw a dream that you were walking among the people in a very rough terrain.

743
00:59:34,972 --> 00:59:36,600
And then you climbed up a mountain

744
00:59:39,525 --> 00:59:42,478
And then you reach on the top of mountain with your companions.

745
00:59:44,491 --> 00:59:49,439
 And then you came down the mountain into a very leveled land.

746
00:59:51,025 --> 00:59:59,476
 With lush vegetation, wonderful trees, many cities and towns

747
00:59:59,553 --> 01:00:07,150
and castles and fortresses, rivers, and then a throne was set for you,

748
01:00:07,216 --> 01:00:11,319
 and you sat on the throne, and then a voice came to you and said,

749
01:00:12,026 --> 01:00:13,778
إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ وَالْفَتْحُ۝

750
01:00:14,993 --> 01:00:19,975
When the victory of Allah, approaches you, then seek forgiveness from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

751
01:00:22,101 --> 01:00:26,323
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) cried and he said: You have given me good news.

752
01:00:26,880 --> 01:00:29,635
And you have also given me my obituary. He said:

753
01:00:31,638 --> 01:00:34,785
The interpretation of the dream and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was very good in interpreting dreams,

754
01:00:34,915 --> 01:00:37,521
 in fact he would interpret dreams at the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

755
01:00:38,310 --> 01:00:40,347
Once one dream was presented to the Rasool Ullah.

756
01:00:40,805 --> 01:00:44,624
Before Rasool Allah ﷺ would interpret the dream Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) interrupted and said:

757
01:00:44,733 --> 01:00:46,153
O Rasool Ullah, allow me to interpret it.

758
01:00:46,781 --> 01:00:47,847
Rasool Ullah said: Go ahead!

759
01:00:48,939 --> 01:00:51,719
So he interpreted it and then he asked Rasool Allah ﷺ  that I get it right.

760
01:00:52,261 --> 01:00:54,644
He said: You get part of it right, and part of it wrong.

761
01:00:54,946 --> 01:00:56,404
 Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Tell me what is wrong?

762
01:00:56,539 --> 01:00:57,582
Rasool Ullah said: I'm not gonna tell you.

763
01:00:59,641 --> 01:01:02,730
But Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) used to interpret dreams and he would love dreams.

764
01:01:04,177 --> 01:01:06,406
And he would always ask the Sahabah(صحابه) about their dreams.

765
01:01:10,606 --> 01:01:15,551
 And by the way, the issue of dreams and Karamat(کرامات)

766
01:01:17,572 --> 01:01:20,451
are something that Allahسبحانه تعالى has given to the Muslims.

767
01:01:22,596 --> 01:01:29,681
But, for example Karamat(کرامات), there are lots of exaggerations in the Karamat(کرامات).

768
01:01:30,656 --> 01:01:37,788
For example one, Karamah(كرامة), that was attributed to, so called Wali(ولي) in Yemen.

769
01:01:39,500 --> 01:01:43,218
It said that he was sitting with his students and then he scratched his arm.

770
01:01:44,201 --> 01:01:46,144
So, his students told him: Why did you scratched your arm?

771
01:01:46,602 --> 01:01:50,542
 He said: Because of one of my Mureed(مريد) has invoked my name in the sea,

772
01:01:51,056 --> 01:01:54,591
 and he was about to drown. So I scratched my arm and he was safe,

773
01:01:56,406 --> 01:01:59,443
obviously you can't buy such a Karamah(كرامة).

774
01:02:00,803 --> 01:02:07,433
So, how could you tell if a Karamah(كرامة) is real or not.

775
01:02:08,433 --> 01:02:13,092
First of all if it has any Shirk(شرك) meaning, then you rule it out.

776
01:02:14,069 --> 01:02:20,413
 Like for example, Abdul Qadir Jilani(عبدالقادرجيلاني), he was traveling once

777
01:02:21,291 --> 01:02:23,366
and he heard a voice calling him from a cloud.

778
01:02:23,956 --> 01:02:29,738
And it said: O Abdul Qadir(عبدالقادر), I am your Lord, and you are my servant!

779
01:02:30,587 --> 01:02:35,044
 And I have relieved you from all of the duties of Islam.

780
01:02:36,689 --> 01:02:40,131
Abdul Qadir Jilani(عبدالقادرجيلاني) said: Shut up you enemy of Allah.!

781
01:02:41,612 --> 01:02:42,860
Shut up you enemy of Allah.!

782
01:02:45,644 --> 01:02:48,188
That was Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) trying to deceive Abdul Qadir Jilani(عبدالقادرجيلاني)

783
01:02:49,174 --> 01:02:51,522
through pretending to be a Karama(كرامة) for him.

784
01:02:51,764 --> 01:02:53,913
 Abdul Qadir Jilani(عبدالقادرجيلاني) told him: Shut up, you enemy of Allah,

785
01:02:54,030 --> 01:02:55,779
this story is narrated by Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه).

786
01:02:57,435 --> 01:02:58,590
So Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) said:

787
01:02:59,087 --> 01:03:02,618
O Abdul Qadir(عبدالقادر) I have deceived so many people.

788
01:03:04,334 --> 01:03:09,922
But you were stronger, and I failed against you.

789
01:03:10,752 --> 01:03:14,449
What did Abdul Qadir(عبدالقادر) say, he said: Shut up, you enemy of Allah.

790
01:03:14,899 --> 01:03:17,821
This is because of Allah is guiding me not because of myself.

791
01:03:19,858 --> 01:03:21,975
So he didn't attribute it to himself, he said: Because of Allah.

792
01:03:22,405 --> 01:03:25,492
Now, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) this same thing that Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) did with

793
01:03:25,508 --> 01:03:27,573
Abdul Qadir Jilani(عبدالقادرجيلاني) , open up the Bible.

794
01:03:28,463 --> 01:03:30,547
 You would find that Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) did it with Paul.

795
01:03:32,173 --> 01:03:35,297
And that was the entire reason for the deviation of Christianity.

796
01:03:35,770 --> 01:03:37,227
He came to Paul and he said:

797
01:03:40,613 --> 01:03:49,158
That all of the laws…. I don't recall the verse itself but what was made illegal on you,

798
01:03:49,551 --> 01:03:51,511
 on everyone is now legal on you.

799
01:03:52,526 --> 01:03:53,692
So the Haram(حرام) is Halal(حلال).

800
01:03:55,055 --> 01:03:58,728
And then Paul says and he told me some unspeakable things  I mean even to Paul.

801
01:03:59,238 --> 01:04:01,869
 He said: He told me some unspeakable things and it says that in the Bible.

802
01:04:02,481 --> 01:04:04,582
But the trick of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) worked against Paul,

803
01:04:05,224 --> 01:04:08,529
but it didn't work against the follower of the Muhammadﷺ, Abdul Qadir Jilani(عبدالقادرجيلاني).

804
01:04:10,985 --> 01:04:14,473
 So how do you tell if a Karamah(كرامة) is real or not.?

805
01:04:16,007 --> 01:04:19,939
There's a key rule, which is a general rule.

806
01:04:22,743 --> 01:04:29,500
Whenever you find that the Karamah(كرامة) is outside of the context of Jihad(جهاد) and persecution,

807
01:04:30,536 --> 01:04:31,685
take it with a grain of salt.

808
01:04:33,399 --> 01:04:40,795
Karamat(کرامات), almost all the time, occur in the context of the Jihad(جهاد) or persecution.

809
01:04:43,415 --> 01:04:45,497
The water, when did it flow out of the hands of Rasool Ullah.?

810
01:04:46,576 --> 01:04:47,499
In Battle of Tabook(تبوك).!

811
01:04:49,661 --> 01:04:56,057
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was invited to a meal, Jabir Ibn Abdullah(جابربن عبدالله) came and whispered to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

812
01:04:56,472 --> 01:04:58,997
 O Rasool Ullah, I have a small goat,

813
01:04:59,702 --> 01:05:05,152
and some barley and I'm going to prepare some food for you, and a small number of your companions.

814
01:05:06,704 --> 01:05:08,581
Rasool Allah ﷺ goes and announces.

815
01:05:10,749 --> 01:05:13,462
All of you are invited to the house of Jabir Ibn Abdullah(جابربن عبدالله).

816
01:05:13,925 --> 01:05:16,457
Jabir(جابر) runs back home and he goes and tells his wife.

817
01:05:17,603 --> 01:05:20,095
You know what's happened.? I mean, he was so embarrassed.

818
01:05:20,501 --> 01:05:22,172
 And you know when you invite people and then

819
01:05:22,239 --> 01:05:24,186
 it turns out to the food is not enough, it's so embarrassing.

820
01:05:24,629 --> 01:05:26,610
And it's even more embarrassing for the wife.

821
01:05:28,081 --> 01:05:32,380
But look at the Momina(مؤمنه) wife she said: Did you tell Rasool Allah ﷺ, the amount of food you have.?

822
01:05:32,804 --> 01:05:36,436
 He said: Yes! She said: Then Rasool Ullah knows better,

823
01:05:37,505 --> 01:05:39,679
 Rasool Ullah knows better! He was so embarrassed.

824
01:05:40,368 --> 01:05:43,181
Came back home rushing, Rasool Allah ﷺ came in and he said:

825
01:05:43,614 --> 01:05:47,640
Don't touch the food, you cook it, but don't put it in the plate. I will do that.

826
01:05:48,674 --> 01:05:51,511
So, Rasool Ullah would bring the soup and mix the bread in it.

827
01:05:52,126 --> 01:05:56,080
And then he would feed the Sahabah(صحابه), the house could only hold 10.

828
01:05:56,417 --> 01:05:57,793
So they would come in, in ten's,

829
01:05:58,263 --> 01:06:02,155
they would eat and leave and then Rasool Allah ﷺ would put food for another ten.

830
01:06:02,515 --> 01:06:05,563
 And then for another ten. You know how many people ate from that food?

831
01:06:06,709 --> 01:06:12,312
800! 800 ate and then Jabir(جابر) says: When Rasool Allah left.

832
01:06:12,814 --> 01:06:17,612
The pot was still overflowing with food. When did that happen?

833
01:06:17,714 --> 01:06:19,053
It happen in the battle of Khandaq(خندق).

834
01:06:21,208 --> 01:06:24,398
So one can go on and on about the Karamat(کرامات), when they happened.

835
01:06:24,622 --> 01:06:25,897
In what context, did they happen.?

836
01:06:26,407 --> 01:06:29,309
 They happen in the context of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

837
01:06:34,426 --> 01:06:36,031
 Also in the context of persecution.

838
01:06:36,229 --> 01:06:44,048
What happened with the Sahabi(صحابي), Khubaib(خبيب).

839
01:06:44,885 --> 01:06:55,986
When his capturer came in and found that he was eating fresh fruits of summer,  in winter.

840
01:06:57,575 --> 01:07:01,889
 So, the Karamah(كرامة) that happened to Maryam عليها السّلام happened to Khubaib(خبيب).

841
01:07:05,579 --> 01:07:06,746
Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني),

842
01:07:09,731 --> 01:07:14,403
Aswad Al-Ansi(أسود ألعنسي),  who claim to prophet in Yemen, he brought Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني).

843
01:07:15,516 --> 01:07:18,360
And he told him: What do you say about Muhammadﷺ ?

844
01:07:19,537 --> 01:07:21,382
He said: I say that he's the Messenger of Allah.

845
01:07:21,974 --> 01:07:24,732
 He said: What do you say about me.? He said: I cannot hear you.

846
01:07:25,638 --> 01:07:27,067
 So he said: What do you say about Muhammadﷺ?

847
01:07:27,541 --> 01:07:29,308
To test him, Did he lost his hearing.

848
01:07:30,207 --> 01:07:33,437
 He said: He's the Messenger of Allah, what do you say about me. I can't hear you.

849
01:07:34,404 --> 01:07:38,793
 So, he know that he's playing games with him. He decided to burn him alive, burn him at the stake.

850
01:07:40,553 --> 01:07:43,894
 They tied him up and they burned him.

851
01:07:45,032 --> 01:07:49,656
Nothing burned except the rope that was tying his hands, he walked out from the fire.

852
01:07:52,916 --> 01:07:53,975
The news spread.

853
01:07:56,887 --> 01:08:00,305
He went to Madina, and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) saw him in the Masjid(مسجد)

854
01:08:00,399 --> 01:08:02,687
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had this ability of Farasah(فراسه).

855
01:08:03,466 --> 01:08:04,504
He can read the face.

856
01:08:05,896 --> 01:08:08,098
So he saw this man and he came to him and he said:

857
01:08:08,642 --> 01:08:11,602
Do you know the servant of Allah in Yemen,

858
01:08:13,049 --> 01:08:16,317
who was burned. And he came out, safe from the fire.

859
01:08:16,644 --> 01:08:17,604
He said: Yes! I know him.

860
01:08:17,707 --> 01:08:19,129
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Is it’s  you?

861
01:08:20,436 --> 01:08:21,779
 He said: Yes, yes! I am!

862
01:08:22,565 --> 01:08:27,018
Umar(عُمَر) hugged him and kissed him and said Al-Hamdullilah(ألحمدلله).

863
01:08:27,624 --> 01:08:32,337
 That Allah did not take away my life until I saw a member of the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ,

864
01:08:32,852 --> 01:08:37,496
 who had the Karamah(كرامة), similar to the miracle that was given to Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

865
01:08:38,488 --> 01:08:42,916
So a member of the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ a Karamah(كرامة) happens to him, similar to the Mujizah(مؤجزة) of Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

866
01:08:43,993 --> 01:08:47,035
 Or Abul Ala Al-Hadhrami(أبوالأعلى ألحضرمي) in Bahrain when he was opening in Al-Bahrain(ألبحرين).

867
01:08:49,191 --> 01:08:56,559
They came into a sea barrier between them and the land they want to cross to.

868
01:08:57,620 --> 01:09:01,801
So Abul Ala Al-Hadhrami(أبوالأعلى ألحضرمي) said: Aren't you the messengers, of messenger of Allah?

869
01:09:01,918 --> 01:09:03,409
 Aren’t you the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),?

870
01:09:03,742 --> 01:09:06,771
make Dua(دُعَا) to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, they make Dua(دُعَا) and then they crossed over the sea.

871
01:09:08,185 --> 01:09:12,414
 Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) says: Only our feet would get soaked with water.

872
01:09:15,017 --> 01:09:17,721
 And there was lines of poetry made on that saying that

873
01:09:18,758 --> 01:09:23,616
you make Dua(دُعَا) to Allah to give you a miracle like the miracle of the ones before, the miracle of Musa(موسى).

874
01:09:24,406 --> 01:09:26,844
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gave you an even greater miracle.

875
01:09:27,477 --> 01:09:30,840
For them, the sea was split for you, you walked over the sea.

876
01:09:33,036 --> 01:09:35,922
But you can notice that all of these Karamat(کرامات) are happening in what context?

877
01:09:36,837 --> 01:09:38,545
 Jihad(جهاد) and prosecution!

878
01:09:40,185 --> 01:09:46,692
With dreams there's more frequency of dreams, with the Mujahideen(مجاهدين),

879
01:09:46,919 --> 01:09:56,231
and with the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) before they die as Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء), because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gives them Tathbeet(تثبيت).

880
01:09:58,707 --> 01:10:00,599
Because of the difficult Fitnah(فِتْنَه) they are in,

881
01:10:00,934 --> 01:10:06,484
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gives them this as a glad tiding, and as a Bushra(بُشرى), and to make them steadfast.

882
01:10:07,602 --> 01:10:11,413
Because when you take that step towards Allah, Allah, takes many steps towards you.

883
01:10:12,433 --> 01:10:15,564
With the mother of Musa(موسى).

884
01:10:18,953 --> 01:10:20,199
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told her:

885
01:10:20,423 --> 01:10:22,373
 If you fear for the safety of your son.

886
01:10:24,167 --> 01:10:25,343
Throw him in the river, right.

887
01:10:25,967 --> 01:10:29,960
وَأَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَى أُمِّ مُوسَى أَنْ أَرْضِعِيهِ فَإِذَا خِفْتِ عَلَيْهِ

888
01:10:30,565 --> 01:10:34,108
 فَأَلْقِيهِ فِي اليَمِّ وَلاَ تَخَافِي وَلاَ تَحْزَنِي

889
01:10:35,545 --> 01:10:39,566
If she's afraid from who, from who? from Firaun(فرعون), right.

890
01:10:40,157 --> 01:10:44,152
 Throw him in the river, so that he could get away from who? From Firaun(فرعون)!

891
01:10:44,384 --> 01:10:50,740
 Where does he go out of all of the palaces and houses lining up the Nile River from both sides.

892
01:10:51,299 --> 01:10:56,138
This boat chooses to dock right next to the palace of Firaun(فرعون).

893
01:10:56,618 --> 01:10:59,668
Now, the mother of Musa(موسى), she was about to give up.

894
01:10:59,722 --> 01:11:03,290
I mean Allah promises me that my son will run away from Firaun(فرعون) and it goes straight to Firaun(فرعون).

895
01:11:03,715 --> 01:11:05,587
 I mean he's gonna run away from the Firaun(فرعون)

896
01:11:05,677 --> 01:11:07,565
and he goes straight to Firaun(فرعون).

897
01:11:08,035 --> 01:11:13,376
She was about to disclose the situation and go to the palace of Firaun(فرعون) and say:

898
01:11:13,745 --> 01:11:16,280
 Give me back my son, and if she did that what would happen?

899
01:11:17,101 --> 01:11:20,189
 They would have known that he belongs to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) and they would have killed him.

900
01:11:20,491 --> 01:11:21,599
 So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

901
01:11:22,093 --> 01:11:27,178
فَارغاً إِن كَادَتْ لَتُبْدِي بِهِ لَوْلا أَن رَّبَطْنَا عَلَى قَلْبِهَا لِتَكُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

902
01:11:27,494 --> 01:11:33,385
She was about to disclose his case, but we intervene and strengthened her heart,

903
01:11:33,824 --> 01:11:35,308
 so that she would be among the believers.

904
01:11:36,136 --> 01:11:40,288
So there was divine intervention to help her in that moment of Fitnah(فِتْنَه). Why?

905
01:11:40,662 --> 01:11:44,575
Because she believed in the Promise of Allah and she took that initial step towards Allah.

906
01:11:45,452 --> 01:11:46,133
 So, the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

907
01:11:46,158 --> 01:11:50,818
because he takes that initial step towards Allah, Allah takes many steps towards him

908
01:11:51,384 --> 01:11:53,034
and gives him Tathbeet(تثبيت) in times of Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

909
01:11:58,564 --> 01:12:03,816
So this is a key rule to use with Karamat(کرامات).

910
01:12:10,668 --> 01:12:12,430
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه  said:

911
01:12:13,084 --> 01:12:17,531
ما ترك قومٌ الجهاد إلًّا عمَّ هُمُ الله بعذاب من عنده

912
01:12:18,124 --> 01:12:23,419
If any people stopped Jihad(جهاد) Allah will covered them all with punishment.

913
01:12:25,778 --> 01:12:29,270
Ibn Asakir(إبن عساكر) narrates that when Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) became Khalifah(خليفه).

914
01:12:30,491 --> 01:12:35,863
 He stood on the pulpit, and among what he said was, the people do not practice Jihad(جهاد),

915
01:12:35,946 --> 01:12:37,787
Allah will inflict them with poverty.

916
01:12:41,078 --> 01:12:45,973
There's no greater revenue for the Islamic Treasury than the Ghanimah(غنيمه) of Harb(حرب).

917
01:12:51,012 --> 01:12:52,606
Forgot to interpret to you,

918
01:12:52,631 --> 01:12:56,099
the dream of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), we wouldn't interpret in terms of dream of interpreting it.

919
01:13:00,843 --> 01:13:02,549
 He interpreted the dream to mean.

920
01:13:04,916 --> 01:13:10,808
When you saw me with people going through a rough terrain, a rocky track.

921
01:13:11,295 --> 01:13:18,955
 That means that we and our enemy will suffer difficulty in this war.

922
01:13:20,380 --> 01:13:23,116
So it's gonna be difficult on us and it's gonna be difficult on the enemy.

923
01:13:23,551 --> 01:13:24,944
It's gonna be a struggle, it's Jihad(جهاد).

924
01:13:26,987 --> 01:13:29,942
 And when you saw me rise with my companions to the top of the mountain.

925
01:13:30,054 --> 01:13:35,629
 It means that in the end, we will prevail, it's difficult, but in the end, we will win.

926
01:13:37,614 --> 01:13:44,380
And then when you saw me, descend onto a fertile valley, palaces, fortresses, rivers, trees.

927
01:13:44,807 --> 01:13:46,866
That means that after this Jihad(جهاد).

928
01:13:47,517 --> 01:13:52,611
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will open to us the earth, and give us these Barakat(بركات).

929
01:13:54,016 --> 01:13:55,721
 So that is a result of Jihad(جهاد).

930
01:13:56,630 --> 01:14:05,410
As a result of Jihad(جهاد), the Muslims would live that life of enjoying the blessings of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

931
01:14:07,176 --> 01:14:10,371
When you saw a throne. And I was sitting on the throne,

932
01:14:10,466 --> 01:14:16,118
it means that Allah will elevate me and Allah will humiliate my enemies.

933
01:14:17,148 --> 01:14:20,090
And when a voice told me, when the victory of Allah comes,

934
01:14:20,662 --> 01:14:24,051
seek forgiveness from Allah, it means that my death is soon.

935
01:14:29,095 --> 01:14:31,407
I told you that the land of Andalus(أندلس) was the land of Jihad(جهاد).

936
01:14:32,864 --> 01:14:38,310
 Brothers the Muslims in Andalus(أندلس) were living a life of extravagance

937
01:14:40,053 --> 01:14:43,095
 that may be the wealthiest man today can't even dream of.

938
01:14:45,696 --> 01:14:51,817
 Yani(يعني), I visited their palaces in their place and I did some research on Andalus(أندلس),

939
01:14:52,769 --> 01:14:54,062
 their lifestyle was amazing.

940
01:14:54,743 --> 01:14:57,540
And that was a result of their Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

941
01:14:59,014 --> 01:15:02,613
They had so much money coming in, they didn't even know, how to use it.

942
01:15:03,818 --> 01:15:15,631
 So, Abdul Rahman As-Salis(عبدالرحمن ألثالث), Qurtba(قرطبه) wasn't enough for him.

943
01:15:17,564 --> 01:15:21,265
 He wanted to build a palace for him but Qurtba(قرطبه) cannot hold him

944
01:15:22,015 --> 01:15:24,383
and Qurtba(قرطبه) at the time was the largest city in Europe.

945
01:15:25,596 --> 01:15:29,663
But Abdul Rahman As-Salis(عبدالرحمن ألثالث), he had 3000 Bodyguards,

946
01:15:30,956 --> 01:15:36,356
 12,000 Servants, 6000 Female concubines with their servants,

947
01:15:37,222 --> 01:15:41,399
so he had to move out of Qurtba(قرطبه) and build his palace, which was called Madina-Tuz-Zahra(مدينة الزهراء),

948
01:15:41,431 --> 01:15:42,994
 the ton of Azahra(ألزهراء).

949
01:15:43,843 --> 01:15:47,832
So, this entire town belong to Abdul Rahman As-Salis(عبدالرحمن ألثالث).

950
01:15:50,342 --> 01:15:53,700
There was so much money coming in that they ended up building their roofs,

951
01:15:54,792 --> 01:15:56,700
the roof of the Diwan(ديوان) was built of gold.

952
01:15:58,160 --> 01:16:02,152
 I'm not saying that that is good that is not, that is extravagance,

953
01:16:02,162 --> 01:16:04,335
that is not approved in this Shariah(شريعة), that is waste.

954
01:16:06,251 --> 01:16:11,579
But I'm bringing this up to say that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ was flooding them with this wealth

955
01:16:11,645 --> 01:16:13,634
 as a result of their Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

956
01:16:14,227 --> 01:16:17,323
They didn't use that those resources right.

957
01:16:18,707 --> 01:16:22,862
Umar Ibn Abdul Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز), when the money was coming in, he would it out to pave roads,

958
01:16:23,070 --> 01:16:25,548
to free slaves, he was putting it to good use.

959
01:16:29,924 --> 01:16:35,120
 So, Jihad(جهاد) brings you Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

960
01:16:35,724 --> 01:16:38,372
Without you running after it Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) would run after you.

961
01:16:39,211 --> 01:16:40,417
Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

962
01:16:41,494 --> 01:16:47,446
وَمَنْ كَانَتْ الدُّنْيَا هَمَّهُ، شَتَّتَ الله شَمْلَه وَجَعَلَ فَقْرَهُ بَيْنَ عَيْنَيْهِ،

963
01:16:47,963 --> 01:16:50,602
وَلَمْ يَأْتِهِ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا إِلَّا مَا كُتِبَ  لَهُ ،

964
01:16:51,191 --> 01:16:57,922
مَنْ كَانَ هَمُّهُ الْآخِرَةَ، ..... جَمَعَ اللهُ شَمْلَهُ،

965
01:16:58,735 --> 01:17:01,636
وَجَعَلَ غِنَاهُ فِي قَلْبِهِ، وَأَتَتْهُ الدُّنْيَا وَهِيَ رَاغِمَةٌ،

966
01:17:02,545 --> 01:17:06,486
If your concern is this life, then Allah will not give you a peace of mind.

967
01:17:07,303 --> 01:17:09,711
 And Allah will place poverty between your eyes,

968
01:17:09,990 --> 01:17:12,364
and you will only get from Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) what is destined for you.

969
01:17:13,613 --> 01:17:16,685
You won't have a peace of mind, your mind will be scattered all over the place.

970
01:17:17,717 --> 01:17:20,313
 You will be carrying your poverty with you between your eyes,

971
01:17:21,117 --> 01:17:24,421
even if you have so much money, you would still feel poor,

972
01:17:25,000 --> 01:17:27,026
 and you're only going to get what was destined for you.

973
01:17:27,349 --> 01:17:29,683
If your concern is Akhirah(آخرة), then Allah will give you a peace of mind.

974
01:17:30,598 --> 01:17:32,810
 And Allah will give you contentment in your heart, wealth.

975
01:17:33,708 --> 01:17:36,869
And this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) will be forced to come to you and follow you.

976
01:17:40,242 --> 01:17:41,896
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

977
01:17:42,131 --> 01:17:44,985
 If people do not practice Jihad(جهاد) Allah will inflict them with poverty.

978
01:17:45,826 --> 01:17:47,371
So Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) comments, he says:

979
01:17:49,036 --> 01:17:53,184
 One might say that I see some people not practicing Jihad(جهاد) nevertheless they're wealthy.

980
01:17:54,863 --> 01:17:57,333
 The answer is that wealth is not the amount of money you have.

981
01:17:58,133 --> 01:18:02,070
Wealth is a feeling of contentment and satisfaction that exists in the heart,

982
01:18:02,978 --> 01:18:06,884
when people stop practicing Jihad(جهاد), they miss out on the booty of war.

983
01:18:07,482 --> 01:18:11,174
When they do that they instead turn their attention and effort

984
01:18:11,347 --> 01:18:13,744
to making wealth from other various means,

985
01:18:15,130 --> 01:18:18,730
they get involved in a lot of prohibited methods of making money.

986
01:18:19,302 --> 01:18:23,445
 You then rarely find anyone among them, whose wealth is pure Halal(حلال),

987
01:18:24,117 --> 01:18:26,945
they become greedy over miser things of this world.

988
01:18:27,602 --> 01:18:31,194
That made them humiliated and they became slaves to money,

989
01:18:32,002 --> 01:18:33,543
but the Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) is free of greed,

990
01:18:33,893 --> 01:18:38,410
and is depending on Allah for his provisions, Allah provides for him from booty.

991
01:18:38,983 --> 01:18:41,282
He wins it, by a sword and it's pure Halal(حلال).

992
01:18:43,449 --> 01:18:48,221
 Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) has so much wealth when he died.

993
01:18:49,365 --> 01:18:51,970
After giving out to all of the heirs.

994
01:18:52,835 --> 01:19:00,740
He decided that he's going to give out part of his will, to every single living Sahabi(صحابي), who attended Badr(بدر).

995
01:19:03,598 --> 01:19:06,072
 I'm talking about Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف),

996
01:19:06,783 --> 01:19:08,381
not Uthman(عثمان), Abdul Rahman Ibn Auf.

997
01:19:11,149 --> 01:19:15,278
So among the ones, who count as the people of Badr(بدر) was Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

998
01:19:15,307 --> 01:19:16,981
even though Uthman(عثمان) didn't attend Badr(بدر).

999
01:19:17,604 --> 01:19:20,211
But Rasool Allah ﷺ counted him as a member of Badr(بدر),

1000
01:19:20,265 --> 01:19:21,746
and gave him part of the Ghanimah(غنيمه) of Badr(بدر),

1001
01:19:22,193 --> 01:19:24,653
because he was told by Rasool Ullah to stay behind with the Ruqaiya(رُقَّيَّه),

1002
01:19:25,421 --> 01:19:26,761
the daughter of Rasool Ullah, who was ill.

1003
01:19:27,527 --> 01:19:28,747
 So when Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) died

1004
01:19:29,358 --> 01:19:34,723
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was presented with this large sum of money,

1005
01:19:35,183 --> 01:19:38,131
and he was told, this is the will of Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف)

1006
01:19:38,209 --> 01:19:43,253
that he gives out part of his inheritance to the ones, who attended Badr(بدر).

1007
01:19:45,019 --> 01:19:48,379
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said: I will accept it from Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف)

1008
01:19:48,447 --> 01:19:50,396
because all of his money is pure Halal(حلال).

1009
01:19:51,409 --> 01:19:56,468
His money is from Ghanaem(غنائم), from business that's Halal(حلال) so he accepted it.

1010
01:19:56,668 --> 01:19:59,575
So, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) the Halal(حلال) you enjoyed even if you're wealthy.

1011
01:19:59,585 --> 01:20:01,072
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was wealthy

1012
01:20:01,153 --> 01:20:04,638
but Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) the Halal(حلال), has a special flavor you can turn it away.

1013
01:20:06,774 --> 01:20:11,220
Now the problem is in these days, Yani(يعني) Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) is saying that

1014
01:20:11,508 --> 01:20:14,573
you rarely find anybody who has Halal(حلال) Rizq(رزق).

1015
01:20:15,934 --> 01:20:22,721
What can one say about Muslims today especially the Muslims living in the West, which is an interest system.

1016
01:20:24,315 --> 01:20:27,136
 So the Ghanimah(غنيمه) is pure Halal(حلال),  Hundred(100)% Halal(حلال).

1017
01:20:27,676 --> 01:20:32,550
 While all of these other means, the least to say, are doubtful.

1018
01:20:37,106 --> 01:20:39,285
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrates that the messengers of Allah said:

1019
01:20:39,750 --> 01:20:44,823
Whoever dies and has not fought or had the intentions of fighting dies on a branch of hypocrisy.

1020
01:20:45,963 --> 01:20:49,405
مَنْ مَاتَ وَلَمْ يَغْزُ وَلَمْ يُحَدِّثْ نَفْسَهُ بِهِ؛ مَاتَ عَلَى شُعْبَةٍ مِنْ نِفَاقٍ

1021
01:20:50,067 --> 01:20:50,934
This is in Muslim(ألمسلم).

1022
01:20:53,001 --> 01:21:00,868
So the ones, who do not have intention of Ghazoo(غزؤ) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عزَّوَجل), are in great danger.

1023
01:21:02,472 --> 01:21:04,543
 Abu Umamah(أبوأمامة) narrates that the Messenger of Allah said:

1024
01:21:05,287 --> 01:21:10,759
Whoever has not fought, or prepared the fighter,  or taken care of a fighter in his absence,

1025
01:21:11,218 --> 01:21:14,017
 Allah will strike him with a disaster before he dies.

1026
01:21:15,037 --> 01:21:16,277
صابع الله بالقارية

1027
01:21:17,533 --> 01:21:21,805
He didn't fight, Prepare a fighter, or take care of his family.

1028
01:21:22,413 --> 01:21:25,273
This Hadith(حديث) is in Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), and it is Hasan(حسن).

1029
01:21:27,094 --> 01:21:28,910
We'll close with that In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله).

1030
01:21:29,013 --> 01:21:31,765
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

1031
01:21:31,861 --> 01:21:33,479
Any questions or comments,

1032
01:21:41,849 --> 01:21:42,279
Yes!

1033
01:21:42,703 --> 01:21:45,249
Question From Audience:

1034
01:21:45,822 --> 01:21:52,210
 Whoever has not fought, or prepared the fighter or taken care of a fighter in his absence.

1035
01:21:53,331 --> 01:21:55,362
 Allah will strike him with a disaster.

1036
01:21:59,237 --> 01:22:03,288
No they consider that,

1037
01:22:03,988 --> 01:22:13,367
even though they were not completely under the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Al-Abbassiyeen(ألعباسين).

1038
01:22:14,165 --> 01:22:17,177
But they did consider themselves to be part of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

1039
01:22:17,930 --> 01:22:20,050
and they will give khut'bah(خطبة) in the name of Khalifah(خليفه).

1040
01:22:33,018 --> 01:22:37,577
Tayeb(طيِّب, In the time of Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّة) it was one Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

1041
01:22:38,471 --> 01:22:40,347
when Banul Abbas(بنوالعباس) took over.

1042
01:22:42,963 --> 01:22:43,995
It was one Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

1043
01:22:45,288 --> 01:22:52,053
And they massacred Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّة), one young man among Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّة),

1044
01:22:52,662 --> 01:22:56,415
Abdur-Rahman Ad-Dakhil(عبدالرحمن ألداخل), he is called the Falcon of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

1045
01:22:58,569 --> 01:23:05,771
he disguised himself in the clothes of a woman, and ran away with his brother,

1046
01:23:06,796 --> 01:23:08,376
and went into hiding in Baghdad(بغداد).

1047
01:23:10,814 --> 01:23:16,671
The soldiers of Banul Abbas(بنوالعباس) did figure out his whereabouts.

1048
01:23:17,485 --> 01:23:21,156
So he ran away with his brother and they tried to cross the Euphrates River.

1049
01:23:23,186 --> 01:23:24,968
 They had to swim Euphrates River.

1050
01:23:25,080 --> 01:23:28,679
And so in Euphrates rivers and some segments of it, is difficult, it's very wide.

1051
01:23:29,743 --> 01:23:32,700
I mean Saddam Hussein(صدام حسين) was proud that he made it.

1052
01:23:34,479 --> 01:23:42,020
 And you know there was big deal on TV the helicopters were taking live footage of Saddam(صدام)

1053
01:23:42,059 --> 01:23:46,703
 trying to cross the river, and then the Americans obviously had comment on that,

1054
01:23:46,918 --> 01:23:50,798
they said: This is not the real Saddam(صدام), this is a look alike.

1055
01:23:52,087 --> 01:23:54,437
So Saddam Hussein(صدام حسين) responded back by saying,

1056
01:23:54,966 --> 01:23:58,075
 crossing a Euphrates River can only be done by the real Saddam(صدام),

1057
01:23:59,000 --> 01:24:01,668
 it can't be done by his look alike.

1058
01:24:02,443 --> 01:24:06,994
So it was a big thing back and forth between them, just crossing the Euphrates River is not an easy thing.

1059
01:24:08,226 --> 01:24:10,911
So Abdur-Rahman Ad-Dakhil(عبدالرحمن ألداخل) and his brother are swimming.

1060
01:24:12,650 --> 01:24:18,423
 And the soldiers of Banul Abbas(بنوالعباس) are on the riverbanks and they're calling them back,

1061
01:24:18,545 --> 01:24:21,161
they're saying don't worry, just come back! Come back! We're not going to kill you!

1062
01:24:21,259 --> 01:24:22,083
We're Not gonna harm you!

1063
01:24:22,832 --> 01:24:27,663
And you know how tempting it is, when you're very difficult and you're exhausted and tired.

1064
01:24:28,139 --> 01:24:30,205
You tried to fool yourself to believe what they said:

1065
01:24:31,734 --> 01:24:33,883
So Abdul Rahman(عبدالرحمن) was telling his brother: Don't believe them,

1066
01:24:34,070 --> 01:24:37,574
they're lying.! Don't believe them! His brother was 13 years old.

1067
01:24:38,511 --> 01:24:40,234
He turned around and went to them.

1068
01:24:40,421 --> 01:24:44,578
Abdur-Rahman Ad-Dakhil(عبدالرحمن ألداخل) saw him then beheading his brother in front of him.

1069
01:24:45,004 --> 01:24:46,415
 As soon as, he arrived they beheaded him.

1070
01:24:47,182 --> 01:24:49,830
Abdur-Rahman Ad-Dakhil(عبدالرحمن ألداخل) ran away from Baghdad and he went to North Africa

1071
01:24:49,933 --> 01:24:53,936
and he was in hiding for four years from house to house, in North Africa, look at the Sabr(صبر), he had.

1072
01:24:55,622 --> 01:24:57,650
 And then he crossed into Spain.

1073
01:24:58,394 --> 01:25:01,174
 He heard that while there was some fitan(فتن) going on so he crossed there.

1074
01:25:01,936 --> 01:25:05,692
 He went to Spain, within one year, he was ruling over Qurtuba(قرطبة).

1075
01:25:07,565 --> 01:25:12,816
Imagine a man entering alone, with no support, no help, it's just him, within one year.

1076
01:25:13,383 --> 01:25:14,773
He was ruling over Qurtuba(قرطبة).

1077
01:25:14,996 --> 01:25:19,228
 Within a few years he was ruling over the entire Iberian Peninsula.

1078
01:25:25,603 --> 01:25:30,994
He was ruling it independently. But he never dared to declare Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

1079
01:25:32,339 --> 01:25:37,187
 he stills submitted that the Khalifah(خليفه) is in Baghdad and that carried on.

1080
01:25:38,706 --> 01:25:43,196
Among his descendants. They were completely independent, but they never declared themselves Khalifah(خليفه),

1081
01:25:43,511 --> 01:25:44,645
 they were called Sultan(سلطان),

1082
01:25:46,592 --> 01:25:55,239
 until one of the Shia(شيعة), Rafidha(رافضة), in Iran declared himself a Khalifah(خليفه),

1083
01:25:55,830 --> 01:25:59,200
 immediately after that, Abdur Rahman As-Salith(عبدالرحمنألثالث) in Spain

1084
01:25:59,336 --> 01:26:02,297
 declared himself Khalifah(خليفه). Why? Because he's not the second,

1085
01:26:03,531 --> 01:26:07,290
the second according to the Hadith(حديث) who should be killed, is the one in Iran.

1086
01:26:08,988 --> 01:26:13,175
So, he took the opportunity and he announced Khilafah(خِلَافَه) in Spain.

1087
01:26:13,644 --> 01:26:15,758
That's also tells us something about the Muslims in Spain.

1088
01:26:16,365 --> 01:26:25,500
They're so wealthy, so confident that they would declare themselves a Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

1089
01:26:25,984 --> 01:26:28,341
One small state declares itself Khalifah(خليفه).

1090
01:26:28,886 --> 01:26:39,519
 And it was quite a strong Khilafah(خِلَافَه), Yani(يعني) in terms of Qurtuba(قرطبة),

1091
01:26:39,638 --> 01:26:41,711
Qurtuba(قرطبة) was the center of knowledge.

1092
01:26:43,148 --> 01:26:48,349
They were fighting against the Romans.

1093
01:26:49,214 --> 01:26:52,619
They were expanding, at least in that era.

1094
01:26:53,510 --> 01:26:56,162
But the thing is that the one who broke the rule,

1095
01:26:56,291 --> 01:27:00,503
let go back to your question, divert to an exit.

1096
01:27:01,628 --> 01:27:05,201
The one who declared the second Khilafah(خِلَافَه) wasn't among the Sunnah(سنة).

1097
01:27:06,996 --> 01:27:11,467
That's how the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) was broken, It was among the Rafidah(رافضي).

1098
01:27:14,270 --> 01:27:17,397
But other than that the Muslims did have respect to the Khalifah(خليفه)

1099
01:27:17,476 --> 01:27:20,829
even if it was a nominal ceremonial position.

1100
01:27:21,085 --> 01:27:23,124
 Later on, Banu Abbas(بنوالعباس) was very weak,

1101
01:27:23,872 --> 01:27:27,149
 but they still recognize that they should only be one Khalifah(خليفه).

1102
01:27:29,029 --> 01:27:32,153
Question From Audience:

1103
01:27:33,356 --> 01:27:38,842
Muhammad Ibn Abdul Wahab(محمدإبن عبدالوهاب), There are some letters that indicate that his Baiyah(بَيْعة) was to Khalifah(خليفه) of Istanbol(إستنبول),

1104
01:27:39,402 --> 01:27:43,868
 and he did not declare that Saudia(سعودية) was an independent state.

1105
01:27:44,442 --> 01:27:46,154
They used to rule it independently.

1106
01:27:46,233 --> 01:27:48,390
They didn't want the Ottomans interfere in their internal affairs,

1107
01:27:48,974 --> 01:27:50,574
but they did not declare Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

1108
01:27:51,024 --> 01:27:53,618
 And they consider themselves to be under the Khalifah(خليفه) of Istanbol(إستنبول).

1109
01:27:56,066 --> 01:27:59,434
And there's actual letter written by Sh. Muhammad Ibn Abdul Wahab(محمدإبن عبدالوهاب),

1110
01:27:59,901 --> 01:28:07,354
stating, he's refuting the claims of people who say that he has succeeded

1111
01:28:07,763 --> 01:28:12,608
and in Khilafah(خِلَافَه), he said that our Baiyah(بَيْعة) is to you and he was very straightforward.

1112
01:28:28,090 --> 01:28:31,624
 That's a commentary by Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس),

1113
01:28:32,467 --> 01:28:34,888
 but the Hadith(حديث) says: Allah will not elevate,

1114
01:28:35,362 --> 01:28:37,246
the humiliation until you go back to your Deen(دِيْن).

1115
01:28:41,216 --> 01:28:45,465
So Deen(دِيْن) is Jihad(جهاد), according to the Hadith(حديث),  going back to the Deen(دِيْن) is going back to Jihad(جهاد).

1116
01:28:56,829 --> 01:29:01,017
Question From Audience:

1117
01:29:02,716 --> 01:29:09,539
There's a similar issue that was discussed by the scholars regarding prisoner of war,

1118
01:29:09,780 --> 01:29:14,861
 who kills himself because he fears for the safety of his brothers

1119
01:29:14,950 --> 01:29:16,706
because of the information that he has.

1120
01:29:17,642 --> 01:29:32,644
And the Scholars said that, if he feels that it's most likely that he will not be able to have patience,

1121
01:29:33,636 --> 01:29:36,701
 and the information that he has can danger the lives of others.

1122
01:29:36,891 --> 01:29:42,417
It's not just physical harm, it's their lives, is allowed for such a person to take away their life.

1123
01:29:44,797 --> 01:29:47,503
 Regarding this situation of women.

1124
01:29:48,953 --> 01:29:53,009
I have not come across, so I cannot comment on it.

1125
01:30:01,648 --> 01:30:05,987
That's regarding suicide and suicide is a matter of an intention,

1126
01:30:06,636 --> 01:30:10,548
your intention to leave Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is because you do not have,

1127
01:30:10,913 --> 01:30:13,833
you are not accepting the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah on you.

1128
01:30:15,294 --> 01:30:18,875
 And suicide is somebody who is not accepting the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah on them,

1129
01:30:19,239 --> 01:30:23,463
whether it is the Qadar(قَدَر) regarding his financial situation,

1130
01:30:23,677 --> 01:30:27,684
like the people who were throwing themselves from the buildings, when the stock market went down,

1131
01:30:28,010 --> 01:30:30,417
in Hong Kong and Taiwan, they just jump.

1132
01:30:30,864 --> 01:30:35,727
They're unsatisfied with the decree of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ regarding the stock market,

1133
01:30:36,654 --> 01:30:41,701
or like the man in Ghazwa(غزوة) Uhud(أحَد),

1134
01:30:42,172 --> 01:30:45,990
who got injured and couldn't sustain the pain.

1135
01:30:46,087 --> 01:30:49,063
So, he ended up jumping over his sword and killed himself,

1136
01:30:50,039 --> 01:30:51,849
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: He is in hellfire.

1137
01:30:52,896 --> 01:30:57,606
So the intention here of taking away one's life wasn't a good intention.

1138
01:30:59,172 --> 01:31:02,725
Now the situation of this woman wouldn't classify as intehaar(إنتحار).

1139
01:31:03,430 --> 01:31:07,274
But would it be a sin. That's question but it won't be intehaar(إنتحار)

1140
01:31:07,386 --> 01:31:10,520
because the intention here is to save herself from sin.

1141
01:31:11,544 --> 01:31:13,960
It's not because she's not pleased with Qadar(قَدَر),of Allah عَزَّوَجَل

1142
01:31:14,465 --> 01:31:18,835
 it is for a valid concern, you seen the difference.

1143
01:31:19,854 --> 01:31:21,521
Question From Audience:

1144
01:31:22,020 --> 01:31:30,658
The issue is not… What is that?

1145
01:31:34,190 --> 01:31:35,179
But it's the sin.

1146
01:31:40,134 --> 01:31:42,468
Yeah, but the intention here is to get away from the sin.

1147
01:31:42,990 --> 01:31:47,416
And when I say, the Qadar(قَدَر) what I meant with Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah, is an issue is of Rizq(رزق).

1148
01:31:49,415 --> 01:31:54,730
Yani(يعني) otherwise suicide bomber will be committing suicide,

1149
01:31:54,840 --> 01:31:56,951
because their intention was to take away their life.

1150
01:31:57,890 --> 01:32:00,931
 But here the intention, what makes it Shahadah(شَهَادَة) is,

1151
01:32:01,049 --> 01:32:02,850
 the intention was done for the sake of Allah.

1152
01:32:18,149 --> 01:32:20,141
Yeah, there's no Tad'di(تعدي),

1153
01:32:21,189 --> 01:32:24,868
Yani(يعني) if a person doesn't pray, it won't accept their other Ibadaat(عبادات)

1154
01:32:24,935 --> 01:32:29,487
 if the person is not fasting it won't affect the other Ibadaat(عبادات),

1155
01:32:29,607 --> 01:32:30,875
 every Ibadah(عبادة) is independent.

1156
01:32:31,448 --> 01:32:36,264
But let me rephrase that, except with the opinion of those who consider neglecting Salah(صلاة) to be Kuffr(كفر).

1157
01:32:37,109 --> 01:32:41,269
 And if one would go with the opinion, not praying is Kuffr(كفر)

1158
01:32:41,365 --> 01:32:43,619
then everything else that is done won't be accepted.

1159
01:32:44,212 --> 01:32:49,609
Other than that, any Ibadah(عبادة) that is a sin, won't spill over something else.

1160
01:32:50,363 --> 01:32:52,177
So a person is not making Jihad(جهاد).

1161
01:32:52,851 --> 01:32:56,411
This sin is within that category, everything else is accepted.

1162
01:32:56,725 --> 01:32:57,764
Question From Audience:

1163
01:33:01,104 --> 01:33:05,064
 when Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) from Makkah to Madina.

1164
01:33:06,932 --> 01:33:14,295
Madina was the only Islamic State and Rasool Allah ﷺ has made Hijrah(هجرة)

1165
01:33:14,473 --> 01:33:17,906
to Madina mandatory.

1166
01:33:19,047 --> 01:33:20,286
When Makkah was opened,

1167
01:33:20,586 --> 01:33:24,077
now you have Makkah is Dar-Us-Salam(دارالسلام), Madina is Dar-Us-Salam(دارالسلام)

1168
01:33:24,118 --> 01:33:25,938
so it's not mandatory to go to Madina.

1169
01:33:26,262 --> 01:33:28,642
However the Muslims should be within the Muslim territory.

1170
01:33:29,763 --> 01:33:32,227
either Makkah or Madina or the areas in between.

1171
01:33:33,818 --> 01:33:39,873
So whenever there's Islamic territory, when there's Dar-Us-Salam(دارالسلام).

1172
01:33:40,583 --> 01:33:44,644
Muslims of Dar-Ul-Harb(دارالحرب) should make Hijrah(هجرة) to Dar-Us-Salam(دارالسلام).

1173
01:33:47,598 --> 01:33:53,634
Relating back to the situation of the Imarah(إمارة) of Afghanistan.

1174
01:33:56,711 --> 01:34:04,922
To say that it will be right upon everybody to make to Hijrah(هجرة) to Afghanistan.

1175
01:34:04,972 --> 01:34:09,068
First of all, there must be an invitation by the Imarah(إمارة).

1176
01:34:10,150 --> 01:34:11,744
For the Muslims to Make Hijrah(هجرة).

1177
01:34:12,538 --> 01:34:16,060
Rasool Allah ﷺ invited the Muslims to the make Hijrah(هجرة) to Dar-Us-Salam(دارالسلام).

1178
01:34:17,931 --> 01:34:23,565
If there is no official invitation, then the Hijrah(هجرة) would not be right

1179
01:34:24,027 --> 01:34:27,227
because what makes the Hijrah(هجرة) Wajib(واجب) is the order of the Ameer(أمير).

1180
01:34:29,045 --> 01:34:33,303
Unless the Ameer(أمير) would make that invitation would make it Wajib(واجب), it doesn't become Wajib(واجب) or Fardh(فرض) on the Muslims.

1181
01:34:36,786 --> 01:34:38,074
Question From Audience:

1182
01:34:38,746 --> 01:34:43,831
I think what you're talking about is not necessarily prerequisites in the terms that I meant, but it's preparations for Jihad(جهاد).

1183
01:34:45,779 --> 01:34:50,052
The Jama'ah(جماعة) of Ameer(أمير) can require preparations for Jihad(جهاد),

1184
01:34:50,958 --> 01:34:54,509
 financial preparations, it's physical preparations, it's training preparations.

1185
01:34:55,612 --> 01:34:57,148
 To this extent that can be required.

1186
01:34:58,278 --> 01:35:03,063
You don't just take somebody off the street doesn't even know how to hold a weapon,

1187
01:35:03,363 --> 01:35:05,063
and ask him to go to the front line.

1188
01:35:05,932 --> 01:35:14,538
 But what I was referring to is saying that you cannot get into the realm of Jihad(جهاد)

1189
01:35:15,340 --> 01:35:20,155
unless you have reached a certain spiritual level.

1190
01:35:21,386 --> 01:35:26,412
And most of the time the spiritual level is an idealistic level that is unrealistic.

1191
01:35:27,588 --> 01:35:28,588
 That is what I mean.

1192
01:35:29,026 --> 01:35:33,652
Yani(يعني) Rasool Allah ﷺ and the people would come and they know how to use their weapons.

1193
01:35:34,486 --> 01:35:36,641
 They are financially ready to join in.

1194
01:35:37,137 --> 01:35:38,678
So in that regard, they are already.

1195
01:35:39,628 --> 01:35:42,792
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not demand that to go for any Tarbiyah(تربيعة),

1196
01:35:43,034 --> 01:35:45,066
Islamic Tarbiyah(تربيعة) to join.

1197
01:35:45,394 --> 01:35:52,163
Why? Because in a certain sense, there is no school of Tarbiyah(تربيعة)

1198
01:35:53,088 --> 01:35:54,520
better than Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1199
01:35:55,577 --> 01:35:59,770
There is no way you could learn about patience better than Jihad(جهاد),

1200
01:36:00,085 --> 01:36:02,609
there's no way to learn about sacrifice, but then Jihad(جهاد).

1201
01:36:03,293 --> 01:36:05,497
There is no way you can learn about The Amal Al- Qalb(أعمال ألقلب),

1202
01:36:05,623 --> 01:36:13,382
like Tawaqqal(توكل) in Allah, having Husn Ul-Zann(حسن الظن) in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

1203
01:36:14,789 --> 01:36:16,342
all of these are Amaal-Al-Qalb(أعمال ألقلب),

1204
01:36:16,431 --> 01:36:19,086
Khauf(خوف) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ like in the battlefield,

1205
01:36:19,774 --> 01:36:23,385
no school can teach you that, no book can teach you that, no Shaikh(شيخ) can provide you that.

1206
01:36:29,519 --> 01:36:33,714
سبحانك اللهم وبحمدك نشهد و الله إله إلَّا أنت نستغفرك ونتوب عليك

